2 TITL Mary Queal Beyer, "A Genealogical History of the French and Allied Families," (Cedar Rapids, IA: The Torch Press, 1912), 22-62.
3 CONT Mary Queal Beyer, "A Genealogical History of the French and Allied Families," (Cedar Rapids, IA: The Torch Press, 1912), 22-62.
3 CONT 
3 CONT VI. Jacob, born in Cambridge March 16, 1640; lived in Billerica on the "east road" near the home of his brother John. His house was one of the garrisons of 1675, and was probably the same building which according to Hazen's History of Billerica, wa
3 CONC s occupied by James Fletcher in that year. He was a sergeant in the militia. He married September 20, 1665, Mary, daughter of Richard Champney, ruling elder of Cambridge church. To them were born ten children:
3 CONT 
3 CONT 1. Jacob, born in Billerica February 20, 1667; died 1700. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT 2. William, born in Billerica July 18, 1668; married Sarah Danforth May 22, 1695. To them were born twelve children:
3 CONT 
3 CONT a. Jacob, born in Billerica May 16, 1696; married May 29, 1722, Elizabeth Davis. To them were born eight children. Elizabeth died February 3, 1738. Jacob married (second) May 19, 1741, Sarah Brown. To them were born four children. Sarah died Augus
3 CONC t 16, 1765. Jacob married (third) November 19, 1766, Mrs. Mary Curtis, who died September 19, 1769. Jacob French died March 7, 1775. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT b. Joseph, born in Billerica January 26, 1698; died February 13, 1698. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT c. Sarah, born in Billerica December 29, 1698; married Nathaniel Whittemore. Sarah died August 15, 1734. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT d. William, born in Billerica January 25, 1701; married January 22, 1727, Joanna Hill, who died January 17, 1769. William married (second) November 27, 1770, Mrs. Mehitable Mooar. William was the father of eleven children. He died April 9, 1776.
3 CONT 
3 CONT e. Jonathan, born in Billerica January 25, 1703; died March 9, 1728. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT f. Elizabeth, born in Billerica April 3, 1705; married February 3, 1730, Josiah Crosby. Elizabeth died November 27, 1739. The husband's death occurred a few years later.
3 CONT 
3 CONT g. Ebenezer, born in Billerica August 5, 1707; married August 27, 1729, Elizabeth Hill. To them were born nine children. Elizabeth died March 26, 1786. Ebenezer died December 31, 1791. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT h. Mary, born in Billerica October 7, 1709; married January 16, 1730, Benjamin Manning. To them were born eleven children. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT i. Nicholas, born in Billerica September 5, 171 1 ; married June 5, 1744, Priscilla Mooar (born June 12, 1724). To them were born nine children, by name: Timothy, Priscilla, Nicholas, Isaac, Lucy, Sarah, Jonathan, Sarah (second), David. Priscilla M
3 CONC ooar French died February 18, 1784. Nicholas French died August 20, 1796. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT j. Lydia, born in Billerica April 29, 1714; died August 2, 1731.
3 CONT 
3 CONT k. Esther, born in Billerica May 16, 1716; died July 7, 1736. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT l. Samuel, born in Billerica May 21, 1718; married Elizabeth Barron. To them were born ten children, by name: Mary, Isaac, Elizabeth, Esther, Sarah, Samuel, Lucy, Oliver, Samuel (second), Silas. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT 3. Mary, born in Billerica, October 6, 1669; died November 12, 1669. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT 4. John, born in Billerica October 6, 1670; died December 3, 1670. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT 5. Joseph, born in Billerica May 5, 1673; died September 25, 1676. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT 6. Jabez, born in Billerica September 16, 1674; died at birth. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT 7. Mary (second), born in Billerica March 5, 1676; married December 13, 1695, Jonathan Baldwin. To them were born three sons and two daughters. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT 8. Hannah, born in Billerica October 23, 1677; died at birth. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT 9. Elizabeth, born in Billerica June 8, 1679; married William Manning. To them were born nine children. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT 10. Sarah, born in Billerica March 7, 1681; married Thomas Baldwin. To them were born seven sons and one daughter. Sarah died June 16, 1761. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT Mary Champney, wife of Jacob French, died April 11, 1681. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT Jacob French married (second) Mary Convers of Woburn. 
3 CONT To them was born: 
3 CONT 
3 CONT 11. Abigail, born in Billerica April 20, 1686; died March 29, 1687. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT Mary Convers French died June 18, 1686. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT Jacob French married (third) Mary, who was drowned June 9, 1709. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT Jacob French married (fourth) Ruth, who died November 6, 1730. 
3 CONT 
3 CONT Jacob French was the father of eleven children. He died May 20, 1713.
