2 TITL William French, "New England, The Great Migration and The Great Migration Begins, 1620-1635"
3 CONT Robert Charles Anderson, George F. Sanborn, and Melinde Lutz Sanborn, "The Great Migration: Immigrants to New England 1634-1635," Volume II, C-F (Boston, MA: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2001), 588-593.
3 CONT 
3 CONT WILLIAM FRENCH
3 CONT 
3 CONT ORIGIN: Unknown
3 CONT MIGRATION: 1635 on the Defence
3 CONT FIRST RESIDENCE: Cambridge
3 CONT REMOVES: Billerica 1652
3 CONT 
3 CONT OCCUPATION: Tailor [MLR 1:205-7, 3:38-39].
3 CONT 
3 CONT CHURCH MEMBERSHIP: Admission to Cambridge church prior to 3 March 1635/6 implied by freemanship. In the January 1658/9 list of Cambridge church members are "William French & Elizabeth his wife both members in full communion, Their children[:] Eliza
3 CONC beth now Elliot & now joined at Dedham. Mary baptized in England between 2 and 3 years old at her father's joining. John baptized by Mr. Hooker in Cambridge. Sarah, Jacob, Hannah born and baptized in this Church" [CaChR 7-8].
3 CONT 
3 CONT FREEMAN: 3 March 1635/6 (seventh in a sequence of eleven Cambridge men) [MBCR 1:371].
3 CONT 
3 CONT EDUCATION: William French sent to a friend in England "the relation of one Indian of two years profession, that I took from his own mouth by an interpreter, because he cannot speak or understand one word of English"; this document was then include
3 CONC d in a pamphlet, Strength out of Weakness; or a Glorious Manifestation of the Further Progresse of the Gospel among the Indians of New-England. Held Forth in Sundry Letter from divers Ministers and others...," published in London in 1652 [MHSC 3:4:
3 CONC 192-93]. Signed his will.
3 CONT 
3 CONT OFFICES: Deputy from Billerica to Massachusetts Bay General Court, 19 December 1660, 27 May 1663, 3 August 1664 [MBCR 4:1:449, 4:2:72, 117]
3 CONT 
3 CONT Empowered to marry others in Billerica and Chelmsford, 18 October 1659, 15 May 1667 (Billerica only) [MBCR 4:2:336]. Petit jury, 3 December 1639 [MBCR 1:283].
3 CONT 
3 CONT Admitted to Ancient and Honorable Artillery Company, 1638 [HAHAC 1:60].
3 CONT 
3 CONT Sergeant, 27 September 1642 [MBCR 2:29-30]. Lieutenant, nominated 1 October 1645 [MBCR 2:137] and confirmed 26 May 1647 [MBCR 2:187]. His inventory included an "old musket & gun barrel" valued at 12s.
3 CONT 
3 CONT ESTATE: In the 8 February 1635/6 Cambridge list of "those men who have houses in the town," "Will[iam] French" had one [CaTR 18]. On 6 February 1636/7, William French was granted two acres of land [CaTR 26]. In 1639 William French held two parcel
3 CONC s of land: "bought of Mr. Richard Champnes, one dwelling house & garden"; and "given by the town two acres of land in the New West Field" [CaBOP 66]. By 1639 William French had sold to John Sill "one house with garden and backside in the town" [CaB
3 CONC OP 57].
3 CONT 
3 CONT In the Cambridge land inventory of 6 September 1642, William French held four parcels: "in the town one dwelling house with about half a rood of ground"; "in the New West Field two acres"; "on the south side of Charles River, eight acres more or le
3 CONC ss being the seventh lot in the lower division of lots"; and "in the upper division of those lots eight acres more or less being the three and fiftieth lot there" [CaBOP 100, 331]
3 CONT 
3 CONT In 1645 William French was granted "six acres & half" "on the west side of Monotamye River" [CaBOP 129]; on or soon after 10 December 1646, William French sold to Edward Winship "in the lots beyond Menotomy six acres & half" [CaBOP 132].
3 CONT 
3 CONT On 15 August 1646, William French sold to Andrew Stevenson "four acres of land more or less in New West Field" [CaBOP 130]. On an unknown date, William French held five acres in Fresh Pond Meadow [CaBOP 333].
3 CONT 
3 CONT In the division of "Shaw Shine" on 4 June 1652, "Lt. Will[ia]m French" received Lot #24, 150 acres [CaTR 97].
3 CONT 
3 CONT On 27 February 1654[/5], William French of Cambridge, tailor, sold to Gilbert Crackbone of Cambridge, husbandman, "four acres of land...in a planting field commonly called there West Field" [MLR 3:38-39].
3 CONT 
3 CONT On 10 June 1656, "William French of Cambridge...,tailor," sold to "William Barret of the same place, tailor,...my now mansion house situated in Cambridge before named with about half a rood of land adjoining to the same...,also a barn and outhous
3 CONC e standing on th...
