3 CONT JOSEPH2 CARPENTER (William1 of Providence, RichardA) was born about 1638 (aged 26
3 CONT in 1664), probably at Providence Plantation (not 1635, in England), and died intestate
3 CONT between 15 or 17 February 1682[/3] and 15 March 1683/4 at Musketa Cove (then a
3 CONT plantation in Oyster Bay Township; now the town of Glen Cove, Nassau County), Long
3 CONT Island, Province of New York. He married first, probably at Rehoboth, Plymouth Colony,
3 CONT ca. 1658 (not on 21 April 1659), HANNAH3 CARPENTER, born at Weymouth, Massachusetts
3 CONT Bay Colony, on 3 2nd month [April] 1640 and died not long before 8 June 1673, probably
3 CONT at Musketa Cove, daughter of William2 and Abigail (Briant) Carpenter of Rehoboth. 
