1 OCCU Collier, Mining operations:  Probably one of the original employees of John Bex & Company sent from England to establish the Hammersmith Iron Works in Lynn in 1645.  His principal occupation at the Iron Works was that of collier; that is, he prepar
2 CONC ed the charcoal used in smelting the ore.  He also did many odd jobs.  For all of his recorded life he was connected with mining operations, first at Lynn and later at Rowley Village.
2 DATE from 1645 to 1675
2 NOTE @N2780@
