2 TYPE Note
2 NOTE Description: Thomas was a skilled worker, a collier, having worked in mining from at least 1646-1675.  Suggesting he was born in England and not an indentured servant from Scotland.  The Scottish workers generally contracted with the Works for a pe
3 CONC riof of 3-7 years and were unskilled labor.  See source referenced in Collaborate Section on the workers at the Iron Works.
1 EVEN
2 TYPE Luke+as+possible+original+surname
2 NOTE Description: The name Luke is known in Scotland.  Many workmen at the Iron Works were Scotch prisoners sent to America after the battle of Dunbar in 1651.  Although Thomas was at the Iron Works at its origin in 1643, Scotch origin has been assigne
3 CONC d to Thomas Looke for those reasons.
1 EVEN
