2 PAGE This indenture mentions several owners of the land and of the lease to the land over a 100-year period:
3 CONT 1654 – original patent to Francis Lace
3 CONT Unstated date – Place Powell obtained the land
3 CONT 1710 – Place Powell sold lease to Augustine Smith
3 CONT 1721 – Augustine Smith sold lease to George & William Proctor
3 CONT 1721/2 – George & William Proctor sold lease to William Sarjant
3 CONT Unstated date – William Sarjant sold lease to John Champe
3 CONT 1750 – Honorias Powell, heir apparent to Place Powell who had been missing for years, sold land to John Champe who already had possession of the lease
