2 TITL St. Helena. Cemetery Records 1830–1970
3 CONT The Willets family settlement in Hempstead began in late 1649, following the purchase of land from Native Americans, with Richard Willets identified as a pioneer arriving from England before the mid-1640s. Richard married Mary Washburn, had severa
3 CONC l children, and held various positions within the community, serving as Surveyor of Highways and a Townsman before his death prior to 1665. His descendants included Thomas Willets, who married Dinah Townsend, and Isaac Willets, who married Clemenc
3 CONC e Hallock in 1716.
3 CONT 
3 CONT Dates:
3 CONT 1649
3 CONT 1665 (approximate date of Richard Willets' death)
3 CONT Names and Relationships
3 CONT 
3 CONT Richard Willets [pioneer and husband of Mary Washburn]
3 CONT Mary Washburn [wife of Richard Willets]
3 CONT Thomas Willets [son of Richard Willets, husband of Dinah Townsend]
3 CONT Isaac Willets [son of Richard Willets, husband of Clemence Hallock]
3 CONT Volume: Vol. 11, family
3 CONT 
3 CONT Language: English
3 CONT 
3 CONT Creator:
3 CONT 
3 CONT Daughters of the American Revolution (Louisiana). Genealogical Records Committee
3 CONT 
