1 SOUR @S6245@
2 PAGE CAUTION ERRORS: where this account differs from "The Great Migration Begins," for Robert Coles use the latter. Robert had no dau Elizabeth who md. a Townsend. Had 3 daus who did.
3 CONT 
3 CONT page 54-55; marriage to Mary Hawkhurst, (incorrectly states all children are by Mary Hawkhurst), birth, death, bio, issue
3 CONT 
3 CONT ROBERT COLE was born about 1597/8 at Sudbury, County
3 CONT Suffolk, England, and came to New England in 1630 and in 1633
3 CONT with John Winthrop, Jr. and others, commenced a plantation at
3 CONT Ipswich, Mass., but the following year he removed to Providence,
3 CONT R. I., where he was one of the thirteen original Proprietors of the
3 CONT Providence Plantations in 1636 and one of the twelve original mem
3 CONT bers of the First Baptist Church.
3 CONT On July 27, 1640, he with thirty-eight others signed an agree
3 CONT ment for a form of government. In 1648 he was listed as an inhabi
3 CONT tant of Warwick, R. I.
3 CONT Shortly after his arrival in New England he married Mary
3 CONT Hawkhurst and died in R. I. before Oct. 18, 1655. She was
3 CONT appointed his administratrix in Oct., 1655, and married second,
3 CONT Matthias Hervey and with most of her children removed to Oyster
3 CONT Bay, L. I., where she died in 1656. Issue: John, Deliverance, Daniel, Sarah, Ann, Nathaniel and Robert.
