2 TITL 1730: George Proctor, Charles Burges, Edward PRICE, John PRICE, Eliz Proctor Hume; Series of Deeds
3 CONT Following Wm Armstrong Crozier's Deed Bk B abstracts on p116 of my father's, "Big Red Book", Virginia Co Records Vol 1, the actual deeds with fs Art Intell. very rough, transcriptions are combined into a pdf--p121-p128 here.  Importantly both Edwar
3 CONC d Price (a planter) and John Price sold their 1728 patents, each for 1000 acres, adjacent to one another--both sold to Charles Burges. So the PRICEs relinquished these parcels, Dec 13, 1730--so only had them about 2 years.
