2 NOTE Description: petitioned to be accepted under the New Haven jurisdiction. His will, found on the probate records at Fairfield, is dated January 6th, 1664. He wills to the four boys he brought up, £10 apiece, if they live with any of his children un
3 CONC til they are eighteen years old, the money then to be put out for them until they are twenty years of age. His will names also his wife Judy, sou James, son Jonathan Lockwood and Mary Lockwood, son Peter's three children, and son Joseph's two. Jud
3 CONC y Bowers, his widow, receipts for her widow's portion, March 6th, 1667. His marriage contract with his wife Susannah, widow of Robert Lockwood, of date May 28th, 1661, pledges certain legacies to the children of Robert Lockwood, deceased, and mortg
3 CONC ages his Greenwich lands and "housings." He died in 1666
2 DATE 1664
