1 IMMI ROBERT LOCKWOOD  came from England about 1630 and settled in Watertown, Massachusetts, where six of his ten children were born, and where their births are recorded Came from England in Governor Winthrop's Fleet.  It is probable that all of the nam
2 CONC e of Lockwood in New England are descended from Robert and Edmund, and there is not much doubt but that there is a misnomer of the widow of Edmund in the Court Records of Massachusetts Bay as printed i. p. 134 and Index.  
