2 TYPE Fact
2 NOTE Description: Stayed in Massachusetts for a few years, then moved to Stamford, Connecticut 
1 EVEN
2 TYPE Life Sketch
2 NOTE Description: (1) ROBERT HUSTED, HEUSTIS, HEWSTEDS, HUSTIS, OR HUESTED  PROBABLY WAS BORN IN [PILSDON], DORSET, ENGLAND IN ABOUT 1595, BUT THE PLACE AND DATE AS WELL AS THE NAMES OF HIS PARENTS CANNOT BE ESTABLISHED [Likely Robert Hewsteds & Lucy He
3 CONC wsteds of Pilsdon].  HE  WAS MARRIED TWICE, 1ST TO ANNE MOONE (in 1616) AND 2ND TO ELIZABETH (maiden surname is unknown - NOT Miller).   VIEW BIOGRAPHICAL ITEMS IN STORIES (MEMORIES) FOR THIS RECORD, 9M2F-H7J
3 CONT (2) See: (a)  Biographical & Family Data for Robert Heustis in outstanding historical series, "The Great Migration.....," compiled by Robert Charles Anderson included in a story (Memories) attached to this record.
3 CONT (b) Robert & Wives Ann (Moon) and Elizabeth (_____), Hustis or Huestis, Biographical & Family Data in Article:“Robert Huestis [2nd] of Westchester County: His Ancestry and His Descendants,” by Gordon L. Remington.
3 CONT ​From Find a Grave
3 CONT Robert Hustis probably originated in Pilsdon, Dorsetshire, England. He was likely a brother of Henry Hustis, and a son of Robert Hustis [or Hewsteds], both of Pilsdon.
3 CONT He removed to Bridport, Dorsetshire, England by 1616. 
3 CONT Removed to the parish of Pilsdon, Dorsetshire, England after February 1622, where he was listed on the susidy roll in 1628 as a landholder by copy in Whitchurch Canonicorum Hundred.
3 CONT At the age of 40, Robert Hustis, husbandman, sailed for Boston from Weymouth, Dorsetshire, England after 20 March 1634/35, and later sent for his family.
3 CONT Granted 32 acres in Mount Wollaston, Massachusetts [Braintree, Norfolk, Massachusetts] on 27 January 1640 for 3 shillings an acre.
3 CONT Removed to Greenwich, New Netherland [Old Greenwich, Fairfield, Connecticut] by 18 July 1640.
3 CONT Obtained a grant of 7 acres in Stamford, New Haven Colony in 1642.
3 CONT Bought 31 acres and a home lot in Greenwich on 5 October 1648.
3 CONT On 6 March 1650[/51?], he owned two home lots of 1½ acres each, 23 acres of upland and 7 acres of meadowland in Stamford.
3 CONT He died between the writing of his will on 8 July 1652 and its probate on 4 November 1654
3 CONT 
3 CONT The Last Will & Testament of Robert Heusted the Elder, viz, Namely:
3 CONT 
3 CONT I give unto my sonn Angell all my Lands Lying in Grennich with thee howsing upon it : Also I give unto my sonn Angell a third part of my cattle : I give unto my sonn Robert all my Lands Lying in Stanfford & One Third part of my Cattle With all th
3 CONC e Howsing on the Land this only excepted that my Wiffe is to have being there her Life time & to her Mantanence for her Cattle from ofe the land I give unto my Wiffe one third part of my Cattle with all my household stuff & a stack of Wheat standin
3 CONC g on the land at grenwich onely my sonn Angell is to have 32 bushels of the said Wheat further I give unto my sonn Angell halfe the Tackling belonging to the working Oxen as Cart & plow & other things belonging there unto belonging to gether wit
3 CONC h a Third part of the Corne I have upon the Ground I give unto my sonn Robert the other halfe of the above said Tackling together with a third part of the Corne upon the ground & I give unto my Wiffe the other Third part of the Corne upon the groun
3 CONC d & I give unto my Dafter Ann tenn pounds which my two sonn are to paye her that is to saye Angell 5£ & Robert 5£ also I give unto my sonns all my Deets this Will Datd this 8 day of July 1652
