2 PAGE page 190 - 191
3 CONT FRANCIS WEEKES or WICKES, is first authoritively
3 CONT mentioned in New England in connection with Roger Williams, ac
3 CONT companying him from Salem early in 1636 to the place later called
3 CONT Providence, R. I. He is described as being "a poor young fellow."
3 CONT SEE MORE IN SOURCE LINK
3 CONT His grave is undoubtedly in the little
3 CONT cemetery on the hill behind the homestead to which he alludes in
3 CONT one of his many deeds but the exact spot cannot be now determined.
3 CONT Six generations of his family lie in this place, the last to be buried
3 CONT there being Charles Weekes who died in 1831. He made his will
3 CONT June 25, 1687, the original of which is still extant being owned
3 CONT by Miss Julia Wright of Oyster Bay in 1922.
3 CONT He married before 1640, Elizabeth Luther, who was living in
3 CONT 1673, but deceased at the time he made his will. Her ancestry is
3 CONT not definitely known. Issue : Samuel, Joseph, John, Thomas, James,
3 CONT Daniel, Elizabeth and Ann.
