1 TITL Descendants of William Cash
1 AUTH Notes for WILLIAM CASH:
2 CONT WILLIAM CASH, the progenitor of the southern branch of the CASH Family, first appears in the records of Westmoreland County, Virginia, 30 May 1694, on which date he was sworn as a grand juror. It is clear from the evidence, however, on this date h
2 CONC e owned a large landed estate, therefore probably arrived in that place some years before. It is believed he came to Virginia from England ca 1680, and is therefore referred to by most CASH researchers as "The Emigrant". His date of birth is estima
2 CONC ted as ca 1660. His plantation was situated in Washington Parish, Westmoreland County, but when King George County was formed
2 CONT from part of Westmoreland in 1720, approximately half of this land fell into each county. His first wife is unknown, however he probably first married ca 1688. His first wife probably died ca 1698 and he was then married ca 1699 to Elizabeth, belie
2 CONC ved to have been the daughter of his friend and neighbor John SKINNER, a Quaker. He died in Westmoreland Co
1 REFN 7B82-PZ3
