0 @N139@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Nathan and Betsy Ware Foster were living on Union St. in Boston, Mass. in 1811. In 1814, they lived in a house on the corner of Center St. and Myrtle Court, and in 1820, they moved to Kennards Ave. By 1831, they were living in a house on Spring Str
1 CONC eet Court, Boston. They were still living there in 1840. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Nathan was a truckman and drowned in the Charles River, Jan. 18, 1845. The family records say his body was found in April and in September he was taken to Springfield to be buried. Betsy died at Springfield, Mass.
