0 @N342@ NOTE Sam Becknall's Will.
1 CONT Will Date: 21 August 1819 Wilkes, North Carolina.
1 CONT Probate Date: 1821 Wilkes, North Carolina.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 1. Wife Elisabeth Becknall, one third of estate.
1 CONT 2. Daughter Nancy Camp: $1
1 CONT 3. Son Thomas Becknall: $1
1 CONT 4. Son John Becknall: $1
1 CONT 5. Son Linsfield Becknall: $1
1 CONT 6. Daughter Jane Huland: $1
1 CONT 7. After all above is done, divide equally the rest of the estate between the following:
1 CONT -Benjamin Becknall, Randolph Becknall, Rhoda Brown, Hannah Stanley
1 CONT -Elisabeth's children: Lewis, Larkin, Aseneth, Clara, Dolly.
1 CONT 
1 CONT [The children who received $1 had all apparently moved farther west, into Kentucky and Indiana. The children that were left with part of the estate were all in Wilkes still at the time of the will. Most were there their whole lives.]
1 CONT 
1 CONT -Rachel Mullins
1 CONT 
1 CONT Source created by RecordSeek.com
