0 @N940@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Edward' (Kenelm, Kenelm1), b. 30 Jan., 1680-1, was a farmer, and resided in Rochester. In 1725, together with Ebenezer Lewis, of Barnstable, and Edmund Freeman, of Harwich, he erected ". iron-works, to carry on the making and forging of iron," nea
1 CONC r his dwelling-house, "on the middle branch of the Mattepoisett River." He was selectman, town clerk, town treasurer, justice of the peace and of the quorum; he was also a
1 CONT Major, and was generally known by his military title. He m. Sarah ,
1 CONT who d. 11 Oct., 1767, aged 85. He d. 25 June, 17UO. His children were:—
1 CONT i. Edwakd, b. 6 Nov., 1703 ; a farmer and Captain, resided in Rochester and inherited the homestead. Hem. 14 Dec., 1728, Hannah, dau. of his uncle Kenelm Winslow, of Harwich; she d. 25 Sept., 1745, and he m. I May, 1746, Rachel, dau. of his uncle J
1 CONC osiah Winslow, of Freetown; she d. 28 Dec., 1706,* and he was published 9 Aug., 1767, to Mrs. Hannah Winslow, of DiRhton. He d. 7 May, 1780.
1 CONT ii. Meiiitari.e,- b. 6 May, 1705; m. 12 Feb., 1722-3, Col. Thomas Winslow, son of her uncle Kenelm Winslow, of Harwich, and was living 20 March, 1779.
1 CONT iii. Sahaji, b. 1707 ; m. before 1725, Thomas Lincoln ; he d. in Rochester, 15 June, 1730, aged 30, and she m. 31 May, 1731, James Whitcomb.t of Rochester, and was living in Western (now Warren), 28 Feb., 1771, when dower was assigned to her.
1 CONT • The date 1767, inscribed on her head-stone, is a manifest mistake, if she was then "in the 45th year of her age," and if Capt. Winslow's subsequent publishment is correctly recorded. ,
1 CONT t James Wbitcomh, son of James, was b. at Scitnate, 21 Aug., 1697, and d. at Western (now Warren), in 17G3. His twin-brother, Nathaniel Whitcomb, was b. two days earlier, 19 Aug., 1697, and d. at Hardwick, 18 March, 1772. Both resided several year
1 CONC s in Rochester. Before he was thirty-four years old, James Whitcomb had four wives, three of whom were cousins to each other, as mentioned in the text:—(1) Mercy, dau. of Deacon Samuel Winslow, 15 Aug., 1721; (2) Joanna Spooner. of Dartmouth, 1
1 CONC 2 July, 1727; (3) Mercy, dun. of Cant. Josiah Winslow, published 15 Nov., 1728: (4) Sarah, dau. of Maj. Edward Winslow, 31 May, 1731.
1 CONT iv. Lydia, b. 8 Sept., 1709; m. 10 July, 1729, Dea. James Foster, of Rochester, andd. 7 Jan., 1770. (Her dau. Mary, b. 11 April, 1732, m. 24 Oct., 1754, Col. Timothy Paige, of Hardwick, and d. at New Braintree, 21 July, 1825, aged 93.J
1 CONT v. Mercy, b. 1 Sept., 1712; m. 10 Oct., 1730, Chillingsworth Foster, of Harwich (nowTJrewster), and d. 25 Jan., 1757.
1 CONT vi. Thankful, b. 2 April, 1715; m. 10 April, 1735, Joeephus Hammond, of Rochester, and d. before 2 Oct., 1758.
1 CONT The New England Historical & Genealogical Register and ..., Volume 26
1 CONT ---------
1 CONT From Find A Grave:
1 CONT In the 81st year of his age.
1 CONT During his time in Rochester he had held the offices of selectman, town clerk, town treasurer, justice of the peace. He was a farmer and for a time was engaged in the manufacture of iron.
1 CONT 
