0 @N1000@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT .......It is believed that Esther's maiden name was Miles or Myles.
1 CONT French (Charles N French) is of the opinion that Esther was the daughter of Joseph Miles who came over from London to Boston in 1633 on the ship "Mary and John.".....Commenting further on Esther, wife of Matthew, probably a Miles, this forebearer w
1 CONC as recognized as a "herb" doctor by her neighbors and friends. Also, Esther (or Hester) wife of Matthew, served as midwife on many occasions, as recorded by NY Genealogical and Biographical Record, from records of Rahway and Plainfield NJ. For exam
1 CONC ple, volume 5, pp 164-165, NY Genealogical Biographical Record, an account is given as follows.
1 CONT Bunn, Hester, present as midwife when her grandchild, Benjamin
1 CONT Loofbourrow was born 1705, 1st month, 21st day, to John Loofbourrow and
1 CONT Hannah, his wife.1  This would mean that Esther was still alive in 1705.
1 CONT 
1 CONT The surname "Miles" for Esther is an assumption based on the fact that Matthew and Esther Bunn named a son Miles Bunn.  However, if as I believe Matthew Bunn's mother was Margaret (Miles) Bunn, that would mean that the antecedent for Miles Bunn's g
1 CONC iven name was the surname of his paternal grandmother, not his mother.  The supposition that Esther (_______) Bunn was born a Miles is dealt a blow by the fact that no one seems able to tie her to any particular Miles family in Mass. Bay in the pre
1 CONC -1659 period.  There is no way that she can be the daughter of Joseph and Mary ("Whelan" or "Whelace" (really "Wheelock")) Miles, as Mary did not marry Joseph Wheelock until 1661, by which time Esther (________) Bunn was already a married and a mot
1 CONC her.  Indeed, Mary (Wheelock) Miles was christened 2 September 1631 in Banham, County Norfolk, so she was no more than seven or eight years older than Esther (_______) Bunn and could not possibly have been the latter's mother.
