1 CONT Griffin: Samuell, s. Samuell and Elizabeth, Apr. 30, 1705
0 @N1166@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT There were 6 different Samuel Griffins, all born in the early 1700s, that people tend to get confused about:
1 CONT 1. Samuel Griffen of Killingworth married Mary Beckwith, his parents are not known at this time.
1 CONT (https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/GXBW-T8M)
1 CONT *2. Samuel Griffin III of Gloucester who married Margaret Burnham, was a son of Samuel Griffin Jr. of Ipswich
1 CONT (https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/9X33-K6B)
1 CONT 3. Samuel Griffin of New London who married Ann Avery, was a son of Ebenezer Griffen 
1 CONT (https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/L1S2-K4V)
1 CONT 4. Samuel Griffin of Middletown who married Alice, parents unknown
1 CONT (https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/L6MR-LPH)
1 CONT 5. Samuel Griffin of Charlestown who married Alice Woodwell, parents unknown
1 CONT (https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/GZDJ-PB3)
1 CONT 6. Samuel Griffin of Newbury and Gloucester who married Mary York and Hannah Dane, son of Shemuel Griffin and Mary Gage
1 CONT (https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/KNZG-V86)
1 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT Samuel Griffin married Margaret Burnham only and she is named as his loving wife in his will dated 10 Nov 1785 which was probated 14 Feb 1794. Essex County Probate Case # 11910 for See Samuel Griffen of Gloucester.  So he could not be the Samuel Gr
1 CONC iffin who married Mary York in 1 JAN 1736. Samuel and Margaret have 9 children recorded in vital records. All of them are named in his will except Margaret who must have died before his will was written. He also named his three Woodbury granddaught
1 CONC ers children of his late daughter Betty Griffin and Peter Woodbury. Samuel Griffen of Gloucester in the County of Essex, Massachusetts, Yeoman...I give to my well loved wife Margaret... my son Samuel, Thomas, Nathaniel, daughter Lydia and my son i
1 CONC n law Andrew Haradon, My dau Peggy, Martha, son-in-law Benjamin Conner, my three granddaughters, Betty, Rebecca and Judith daughters of my daughter Betty. I give to Eunice widow and relict of John Cunningham late of Gloucester. Samuel Whittemore, E
1 CONC sq, my son Thomas Griffen and Mr. Jonathan Griffin executors. 10 Nov 1785
1 CONT 
1 CONT I've attached a copy of his will. Maybe someone would like to transcribe the whole will and post it here or on another world tree on the Internet. I may do so myself but not today. The essence of it is above. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT  Massachusetts, Probate Court (Essex County). The Probate Records of Essex County, Massachusetts. (Salem, Massachusetts: The Essex Institute, 1916, 1917, 1920), Samuel Griffen Deacon Case 11910 Gloucester Will 10 Nov 1785 Probate 14 Feb 1794.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Probate:
1 CONT https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/essex-county-ma-probate-file-papers-1638-1881/image?volumeId=13766&pageName=11910:1&rId=245341744
1 CONT 
1 CONT Will:
1 CONT https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/essex-county-ma-probate-file-papers-1638-1881/image?pageName=11910:8&volumeId=13766&rId=30206211
