1 CONT Brookfield
1 CONT Worcester County
1 CONT Massachusetts, USA
1 CONT 
1 CONT Keziah Cooley was the daughter of Benjamin Cooley Jr [1681-1745] and Margaret Bliss [1683-1744]. She was one of eight children: three girls, five boys.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Keziah married Philip Goss III, son of Capt. Philip Goss Jr and Judith Hayward, on 25 Nov 1723 in Brookfield, MA. They had seven children, five lived to adulthood: Philip IV, Hannah, Ebenezer [died young], Keziah, Judith, Nathaniel [died young] an
1 CONC d Thomas.
1 CONT 
1 CONT It's recorded that a "Kesiah Goss" married Timothy Brown on 18 Apr 1744 in Brookfield, MA. He was her husband's 1st cousin [his mother and Philip Goss's mother were sisters]. There is a discrepancy in death dates for Keziah as I've seen the date o
1 CONC f Oct 1744 listed. Still trying to find a reliable record on this.  (Source Find a Grave)
1 CONT 
1 CONT Goss, Kesiah and Timothy Brown, Apr. 18, 1744.*
1 CONT Early Vital Records of Massachusetts
1 CONT From 1600 to 1850, Brookfield Marraiges
1 CONT https://ma-vitalrecords.org/
1 CONT There were no living children of this marriage.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Philip Goss died in 1742 before his father's death. The inventory of his estate was dated 17 Sep 1742 and the distribution was May 1746.  (Source: New England Families, Genealogical and Memorial: A Record of the ..., Volume 2, edited by William Ric
1 CONC hard Cutter)
1 CONT After the death of Philip Goss III in 1742, Keziah (Cooley) Goss, his wife, became the Administrator of the estate of her husband.  Her son, Philip Goss IV took over in about 1745 after the death of his mother Keziah. Philip the III's estate show
1 CONC s that she was referenced as Keziah Brown formerly Keziah Goss.
