0 @N1353@ NOTE New Aberdeen, or, The Scotch Settlement of Monmouth Country, New Jersey
1 CONT 
1 CONT Naturally one would look for some sort of town lots, such as were to be found in Perth Amboy, Middletown or Shresbury, and not long since we were rewarded by find the return for the 100 acres upon which the town of New Aberdeen stood. It bears date
1 CONC , as was to have been expected, some years after the actual settlement. Such was the case also with other towns in Monmouth and elsewhere. In the office of teh Secretary of State in Trenton, Book - - page 438 we find this "Return" "Surveyed and lai
1 CONC d out for (multiple names listed)
1 CONT Alexander Napier and Peter Watson are both listed, among many others. . .  all that one hundred acres of land adjoining upon the south side of teh land late of Andrew Burnet, formerly Thomas Warne's and bounded east by land-lots of Thomas Hart, gra
1 CONC nted to these persons by patent dated June 7, 1701, adjoining lands of Lewis Nesbit.  
1 CONT 
