0 @N1493@ NOTE This is the closest for that name change since it isn't technically a title nor rank. Colonel should be placed under rank
0 @N1494@ NOTE His family was born Parke.
0 @N1495@ NOTE In 17th century colonial America there are not birth notices with suffixes like "of Ballinger's Mountain" . In genealogy we use the most accurate name closest to what primary source we have at the time of birth and everything else is place
1 CONC d under other headings so that each will show this profile if searched but also that proper "hints" can come through with the correct name etc.
1 CONT 
1 CONT   Technically "Colonel" shouldn't be a prefix for this man's name at birth either. Not just because he is a direct great grandfather of mine and I am changing it as many people write but the same rules above apy here. Also,, there is no mention o
1 CONC f any "Colonel" or military ranking on this profile nor is he listed as such on any sources yet attached. I was confused as to why I could no longer find his profile and it appears it was deleted or merged and the names changed so it wouldn't appea
1 CONC r in a search. Not a big deal but explaining it all with hopes it helps someone on their journey in this field. If there is reason to change it or are any questions please message me andI will gladly retract any incorrect statement or explain furth
1 CONC er. Cheers! B.E.S.
