0 @N1569@ NOTE This date is what is inscribed on Ebenezer's gravestone.
0 @N1570@ NOTE Ullmann, “Some Descendants of Roger Billings,” 193-194.
0 @N1571@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT DO **NOT** MERGE WITH HIS HALF BROTHER, G34B-94V.  They are two separate individuals.  The first Ebenezer died before this Ebenezer, LR19-NTN, was born.  Ebenezer had an older brother who died as a child and, as was often customary in those days, t
1 CONC he family reused the name.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT This Ebenezer was the son of Roger and his second wife Hannah, maiden name unknown.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT The source for birth information for Roger's children include the civil vital records of Dorchester, which can be found on ancestry.com, and a collection of the "Records of the First Church at Dorchester ... 1636-1734" which can be found online (an
1 CONC d see attached under Sources).
1 CONT 
1 CONT This Ebenezer has no birth record but was christened Jan. 11, 1655/6 (see page 167) as  "Ebinezer Billindge," as the last name"Billings" was often spelled anciently.   
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ebenezer and his wife Hannah had a large family; some of his children have birth or christening records, as in: 
1 CONT 1.Richard 1677 (baptized at same time as brother Ebinezer)
1 CONT 2.Ebinezer 1677
1 CONT 3.Ziporah 1679
1 CONT 4.Jonathan 1681
1 CONT 5.Elizabeth 1683
1 CONT 6.Hephzibah 1685
1 CONT 7.Mary 1687
1 CONT 8.Benjamin 1689
1 CONT 9.Samuell 1691
1 CONT 
1 CONT In Ebenezer's will, he names:
1 CONT 1. son Richard
1 CONT 2. Ebenezer
1 CONT 3. Jonathan
1 CONT 4. Benjamin
1 CONT 5. Samuel
1 CONT 6. Bariah
1 CONT 7. Bazaleel
1 CONT 8. Elkanah
1 CONT 
1 CONT 9. daughters Zipporah Man
1 CONT 10. Elizabeth Royall
1 CONT 11. Hepsibah Bradish
1 CONT 12. Mercy Billing
1 CONT 13. Hannah Billing
1 CONT 
1 CONT and Indian servant Joseph Obadiah. Beloved wife is mentioned but not named.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Ebenezer Billings is said to have abhorred drunkenness even though he was a very successful tavern keeper. His obituary in the Boston New Letter 3 February 1717/1718 reads, "On the 25th of January dies, here Capt. Ebenezer Billings, Esq: in the 6
1 CONC 3 year of his age, very much Lamented by his Neighbours both of this and the Neighbouring Towns; He was a great Lover of the Religion and Liberties of his country, a great friend to Justice, very diligent to find out,and exact in punishing Vice, es
1 CONC pecially Drunkenness and Sabbath breaking."
