0 @N1606@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT See page 204 of James C. Townsend, "A Memorial of John, Henry and Richard Townsend," (New York: W. A. Townsend, 1865).
1 CONT "Mary, daughter of Henry 1st, married John, son of Nicholas Wright....  Issue, Rose, Eliphal and Mary.
1 CONT Daughter "ROSE, as well as Eliphal, is said to have been a celebrated beauty.  Rose married first, Nathaniel Coles, Jr.  He died September 8, 1704, and she married Justice John Townsend [son of Thomas, son of John 1st].  She became a widow again, i
1 CONC n 1709.  This time she remained unmarried several years, but in 1734 signs herself Rose Birdsall, after which nothing is known of her.  She must have had what was then a handsome fortune from her father, which she was quite competent to manage.  He
1 CONC r writing is remarkably easy and handsome--Issue, by her first husband, Rosannah, Freelove, Martha and Wright; by the second, Penn and Rose.  (See Justice John, Chap. IV.)....
1 CONT "ELIPHAL, daughter of Mary Townsend and John Wright, married, first, Henry Townsend 3rd, by whom she had 2 children, Henry and Absalom.  Her husband died in 1709, and she married Daniel Wright, who only lived one year.  Her third husband was John M
1 CONC orris, of New Jersey, by whom she had three children, Deborah, Justus, and John.  Deborah married Johannus De Camp, near Morristown; and her daughter, name unknown, married a De Hart.  Of Justice we know nothing."
1 CONT "MARY, daughter of Mary Townsend and John Wright, married Richard, son of Josias Latting, and was, through her son Josias, the ancestress of all the Lattings in the Town.  Her second husband was Jacob Furman, probably the son of her aunt (Susanna
1 CONC h Townsend) and Aaron Furman, Jr.  By him she had a daughter, Susannah, who married Thomas Morgan, which is all that is known of her."
