0 @N1636@ NOTE The Last Will and Testament of James Tallman of Portsmouth ... Practitioner in Physick ...
1 CONT I give and bequeath unto my son John Tallman ... all my hundred acre lott of land ... in the Township of Tiverton ... being in number the 11th lott in the first division he the said John Tallman yielding and paying therefore unto my son Jeremiah Ta
1 CONC llman the sum of 500 pounds ... when he shall attain to the age of 21 years, but in case he my said son John shall neglect or refrain to pay the aforesaid sum that then I give and bequeath the one half of the aforesaid lott of land unto my said so
1 CONC n Jeremiah Tallman ..., to be equally divided from East to the West. 
1 CONT I give and bequeath unto my son Peter Tallman ... my fifty acre Lott of land ... in Tiverton ...
1 CONT I give and bequeath unto my son Silas Tallman ... my tract or parcel of land which I purchased of William Cory ... in Tiverton
1 CONT I give and bequeath unto my son Joseph Tallman ... two parcels of land in the township of Portsmouth ... one piece to be of the northward most part of this my homestead ...  The other piece of land is that which I purchased of William Sanford of Ne
1 CONC wport ...
1 CONT I give and bequeath all the rest and remainder of my homestead whereon I dwell unto my son Stephen Tallman ... And also I give unto my said son Stephen one other piece of land containing 30 acres ... in Portsmouth ... . He Therefore paying 200 poun
1 CONC ds currant money to the Trustees of the Colony of Rhode Island and to clear all that land that is mortgaged for the payment of the 200 pounds.  And also to pay unto his sister Jemima Tallman 200 pounds with in six years after my decease.  And als
1 CONC o to pay unto his sister Hannah Tallman 100 pounds when she shall attain to the age of 17 years.
1 CONT I give and bequeath unto my loving wife Hannah Tallman the Profit and Income of all that land given unto my son Joseph Tallman until he shall attain to the age of 21 years.  And also I give unto my sd wife the profit and income of one half of all t
1 CONC hat land giving to my son Stephen with priviledge of one half of the housings to live in with as many of her children as she shall see cause during her widow-hood.  
1 CONT I give and bequeath unto my well beloved wife Hannah Tallman all the rest and residue of my estate whatsoever and wheresoever it is to be found either in the Colony of Rhode Island or in the Province of the Massachusets Bay [Tiverton was then in MA
1 CONC ] in New-England be it in lands goods debts or chattels the same I give unto her ... she paying the sum of 200 pounds  ... unto her and my daughter Mary Tallman.   The above bequest given to my wife I give in lieu of her thirds if she see cause t
1 CONC o accept of the same.
1 CONT Lastly I do hereby nominate ... and ordain my well beloved wife Hannah Tallman my Executrix and my loving friend and nieghbour Daniel Howland my Executor to this my last  Will and Testament.
1 CONT [Further instructions were given in case one or more of his young sons predeceased him.]
1 CONT ... 11 Jan 1723/4
1 CONT Wit: Josiah Arnold, Daniel Anthony, William Anthony               James Tallman
1 CONT Proved: 10 Feb 1723/4.
1 CONT 
1 CONT The inventory "of all and singular the goods and chattels of James Tallman of Portsmouth  in the Colony of Thode Island a practicer in Physick, who deceased the 25th day of ye 11th month [Feb] 1723/4" totaled £1373:16:6.  [This did not include an
1 CONC y real estate.]
1 CONT Inclued in this total was: "Paper Bills of Public Credit   £232:14"; Debts owed to James £287:16:6; Food and Crops £108; animals except horses £186:10; Horses £35; Physican stuff about £8; Saddles, etc £8; 2 guns and a sword £ 4; Tools an
1 CONC d farm impliments £20:10;  a little boat £5; a Negro woman £40.  The rest was household and personal goods and furniture.   
1 CONT Son John sold his land 14 March 1725/6, Bristol Co., MA, Land Book 17, p. 480 [there are three sets of Bristol Co. land records
