1 CONT Adam Mott (1762-1839), a Quaker, was born in North Hempstead Township, Long Island, the son of Adam and Sarah Willis Mott. He married Anne Mott (1768-1852), daughter of James Mott of Mamaroneck, New York, Adam's second cousin, in 1785. They had si
1 CONC x children, 1786-1798. He died at Rochester, New York. Descendants listed lived in New York, Ohio and elsewhere.
1 CONT Includes the Cornell, Hicks, Moore, and other related families.
1 CONT Also includes the ancestry of Adam and Ann Mott Mott and some descendants of their ancestors. Ancestors include: Adam Mott (d. 1690) of Essex England and Hempstead, Long Island; Captain John Underhill (d. 1672) of Killingworth, New York; Captain Th
1 CONC omas Willett (d. 1674) of New York City and Swansey, Plymouth Colony; William Carpenter (1605- 1685) of Amesbury, England, and Providence, Rhode Island; Henry Willis (d. 1714) of Hempstead and Westbury, New York; Robert Titus (fl. 1635-1654) of Reb
1 CONC oboth, Massachusetts, and Huntington, Long Island; and Captain John Seaman (d. 1695) of Salem, Massachusetts, and Hempstead, New York.
