0 @N1836@ NOTE Thomas Burnam aka Burnham
1 CONT Born 27 Jan 1681 in Ipswich, Essex County, Massachusetts Bay Colony
1 CONT Son of James Burnham and Mary (Cogswell) Burnham
1 CONT 
1 CONT Brother of:
1 CONT Mary (Burnham) Tuttle 
1 CONT Joanna (Burnham) Dodge 
1 CONT James Burnham
1 CONT Thomas Burnham
1 CONT 
1 CONT Husband of Margaret (Boardman) Burnam — married 30 Sep 1703 in Ipswich, Essex County, Province of Massachusetts Bay
1 CONT 
1 CONT Children of Thomas and Margaret:
1 CONT Thomas Burnam 1704
1 CONT Margaret Burnam [1709]
1 CONT Joshua Burnam 1710
1 CONT Ophin Burnam 1712
1 CONT Elizabeth Burnam 1715
1 CONT Mary Burnam 1718
1 CONT John Burnam 1722
1 CONT 
1 CONT Died about 9 May 1759 at about age 78 in Ipswich, Essex County, Province of Massachusetts Bay
1 CONT Buried at Old Burying Hill (later called the Highland Cemetery) in Ipswich
1 CONT 
1 CONT Will of Thomas Burnam
1 CONT His will names children Thomas, Joshua, Offen, John (deceased), Margaret Griffen and Mary Peabody. His wife died a few months before he died, and is not mentioned in his will.
1 CONT 
1 CONT In a deed in which Thomas Burnam transferred property to his son John, the following lines appear: "...I, Thomas Burnam of Ipswich... yeoman, for and in Consideration of ye Parental Love and Affection which I have and Do bear toward my son John Bur
1 CONC nam of Ipswich aforesaid, Husbandman... except that I design for my Son Joshua Burnam.... as was allowed by my Hon. Father James Burnam, Dec[ease]d & as I reserve for my Son Joshua Burnam...
1 CONT 
