0 @N1859@ NOTE Thomas Stanton Society
1 CONT  
1 CONT Thomas Stanton Society
1 CONT News
1 CONT Membership
1 CONT History
1 CONT Tour important sites
1 CONT Stanton Davis Homestead Museum
1 CONT Research sources
1 CONT Genealogy
1 CONT 
1 CONT  	
1 CONT 2020 Reunion Announcement
1 CONT 
1 CONT Purpose of the Society (what we are all about)
1 CONT We wish to honor the life and work of Thomas Stanton, colonial founder of Hartford and Stonington, CT. He helped mold and shape their size, shape, and general character. He helped forge a society that preserved and advanced the best of European cul
1 CONC ture while respecting the needs and desires of the local native American population.
1 CONT 
1 CONT The purpose of the organization is to bring together widely spread cousins into a social fabric for the enjoyment of family and local history, and for exchanging information in the pursuit of genealogy and family pedigrees. We hope to instill a jo
1 CONC y in visiting New England and eastern Connecticut. We believe that by studying Thomas Stanton and his compatriots and by viewing his historical sites that we can actually feel the sense of history and its energy. (from Thomas Stanton Newsletter Num
1 CONC ber 3, December 1998.)
1 CONT 
1 CONT President - Rick Stanton [contact Rick]
1 CONT Vice President - Nancy Ryan
1 CONT Secretary and Membership Chairman - Tom Mennillo
1 CONT Treasurer - Donna Amentt
1 CONT 
1 CONT Application for Membership
1 CONT The only requirements for membership are to show your direct lineage to Thomas Stanton and Anna Lord of CT. and the payment of annual dues. Additional details are shown on our Membership page, where you will find the applications for membership.
1 CONT Thomas Stanton Society By-Laws
1 CONT Click here to download the By-Laws as amended at the Annual Membership Meeting October 15, 2016.
