0 @N1887@ NOTE JOHN HUNTING AND HIS DESCENDANTS.  By T. D. Huntting, of Brooklyn, N. Y.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 'Elder John Hunting... was born in Hoxne, a village in Suffolk County, England, about the year 1597...  In Hester Seaborn, his wife -- a cousin of the Martyr John Rogers... During the yer 1638 a number of vessels arrived at Boston bringing... Joh
1 CONC n Hunting, his wife and five children....  it was in the spring of that year when he first settled at Dedham... Most of his children were born in England... Through John, the eldest son, we find the name has been spread to all parts of America.  Th
1 CONC e daughters all married and their descendants are to be found among the Wares, Fishers, Pecks and Buckners of the present day....
1 CONT 
1 CONT MARGARET, the oldest daughter married, March 24, 1645, Robert Ware or Wares...
1 CONT 
1 CONT HESTER married Nathanial Fisher..
1 CONT 
1 CONT MARY married a Buckner and
1 CONT 
1 CONT ELIZABETH married John Pecke of Rehoboth...
1 CONT 
1 CONT JOHN, the son, born about 1628 married Elizabeth Paine, and had ten children of whom the third, Nathaniel moved to East Hampton, N.Y. in 1696.  NATHANIEL was born Nov 15, 1675, graduated from Harvard College in 1693, and married Mary Green, a daugh
1 CONC ter of John and Ruth Green and granddaughter of Percival and Ellen Green, in 1701... failing health compelled him to resign in 1745, and retire to his farm, where he remained until his death Sept 21, 1753...'
