0 @N1940@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT "May Court 1782  The Will of Howard Cash, Decd. presented in Court by Tamsey Cash, widow and Extrix. and Hendrick Arnold and Samuel Higginbotham Exors; proved by the oaths of Caleb Higginbotham, Charles Burrus and Thomas Powell witnesses."
1 CONT Source from
1 CONT Amherst County Virginia in the Revolution
1 CONT Although always referred to as simply Howard Cash in his life time and in the wills of both his father and himself, there is the following deed suggesting he was Robert Howard Cash:
1 CONT Amherst DB E, p.38   7 Sep 1778.   Robert Howard Cash & wife, Tamsey, to Hendrick Arnold, all of Amherst, 545 acres willed to the said Robert of his father Robert Howard Cash, dec'd.  Patented to Robert Cash, 3 Nov 1750, at Williamsburg.
1 CONT Since neither he nor his father ever used the name Robert, the possibility remains that this is an error on the part of the clerk who copied this deed.
1 CONT Named in his father's will as "Howard" in 1708. He was NOT one of the underage children named in the will so was at least 21 years of age in 1708.  He married Ruth in about 1727 in Westmoreland, Colony of  Virginia as well.  There is no documentati
1 CONC on of Ruth's surname.  His will was written on 28 Feb 1772 and submitted for probated on October 6, 1772, in Amherst, Virginia.  He died sometime between those two dates.
