0 @N1946@ NOTE The Will of Howard Cash is in Amherst Co VA Will Book 1, p.228-231:
1 CONT Dated:   28 Feb 1772.  Submitted for probate:  6 Oct 1772.
1 CONT Lend my wife Ruth, eight negroes:  Joseph, Cate, James, Charles, Sall, Dinah, Dick & David.  Also the land and plantation where I live during her natural life or widowhood
1 CONT To son Joel, 100 acres joining the land where he lives and 2 slaves.  And to my grandson Howard, son of Joel, after the death of Joel.
1 CONT To dau Mary Lively, slave Sarah
1 CONT To son Benjamin, 400 acres adjacent the property of Capt. Aaron Higginbotham, and the land where I live.  Also fellow James whom I purchased of W. Thomas Mitchell
1 CONT Lend to dau Rosanna, slave Fillis and after Rosanna's decease to my grandson Micajah
1 CONT Lend to dau Ann Powell, slave Peg and after her decease to her heirs; if she has no issue, the increase to descend to the childron of Rosanna
1 CONT To son Robert, 240 acres between the land where I live and Stephen Cash's land.  Also the 400 acres which I left to my wife, after her decease; a boy John, bed & furniture and 2 cows
1 CONT To dau Mary Ann, boy Ralph, a bed & furniture and a cow & calf
1 CONT My dau Elizabeth Nuckles may have 30£ to be raised out of my estate to be paid in ten years, by an order for 3£ per year upon some merchant
1 CONT To dau Ruth, girl named Nell, also bed & furniture and cow & calf
1 CONT To son Stephen, 5 sh.
1 CONT To daughter Sarah Mauze [Mayse], 5 sh
1 CONT After decease of wife Ruth, James & Charles descend to son Joel; Joseph & Cate to son Benjamin; Sall & Davie to son Robert
1 CONT After the decease of me and my wife, the increase of Sall is to be divided between daughters Mary Ann and Ruth
1 CONT Any residue to my wife during her life and after to be divided equally between sons Joel, Benjamin & Robert.
1 CONT I do not desire the estate be appriased; wife to be executrix and sons Joel, Benjamin & Robert, executors.
1 CONT Signed:  Howard Cash
1 CONT Wit:  Roderick McCulloch, David Crawford
1 CONT 
1 CONT Presented for probate on 6 Oct 1772.  Proved by oaths of witnesses.  Certificate granted Ruth Cash, Joel, Benjamin & Robert Cash.  Securities with Richard Powell and Gabriel Penn.
