1 CONT His parents, Thomas Fisher and Elizabeth Allin, were from England.
1 CONT His mother was probably pregnant on the voyage in 1634. Samuel was born soon after their arrival in Cambridge, Mass.
1 CONT 
1 CONT In 1671 Rev. John Allin, in his will dated 1671, bequeated to his kinsman, Samuel Fisher, his Wrentham land.
1 CONT Allin was his mother's brother. See Find A Grave Memorial# 21096704
1 CONT He was the first deacon chosen in Wrentham in 1672.
1 CONT He was a representative from Wrentham, Mass., 1689-92
1 CONT 
1 CONT Married 1659 to Meletiah Snow.
1 CONT Children were:
1 CONT Meletia Metcalf
1 CONT Hannah Fisher
1 CONT Ebenezer Fisher
1 CONT Samuel Fisher
1 CONT Abigail Fisher
1 CONT Sarah Fisher
1 CONT Mehitable Fisher
1 CONT ∼
1 CONT SAMUEL, son of Thomas & Elizabeth (Allen) Fisher, was born about 1634.
1 CONT He married at Boston 22 March 165[8/]9 "Milcha [Meletiah] Snow, daughter of Thomas Snow of Boston."
1 CONT 
1 CONT Massachusetts death records give death date as 5 Jan 1702.
