0 @N2005@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Moses 5th son and 8th child, born in Stamford, CT. 1645. He was a blacksmith and lived in Stamford as late as 1701. He owned land in both Stamford and Greenwich, which he rec's from his father by his will (will dated 15 Apr 1670, actually will say
1 CONC s 'My house and land in Stamford w/ all the upland and meadows belonging to me'. No mention of Greenwich). He never lived in Greenwich. He was admitted freeman in Stamford May 1670, was also one of 75 persons who drew land by lot in 1699. In 1701
1 CONC , a settlement of the wealth of the town being made, he was credited with 45L,5s. He soon after this moved to Peekskill, NY where he lived to be a very old man. He died in 1756. He m. 1669 Miss Abigail Westcott, dght of Richard Westcott of Stamford
1 CONC , CT.  (Children: Abigail, Israel, Jonah, Mary, Moses) Source: Knap Knapp family genealogy, Charles Ruggle Knapp, 1903Ancestry
