0 @N2081@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT According to Robert Charles Anderson of the Great Migration Project and every other genealogist who has written about this family:
1 CONT 
1 CONT Samuel3 Griffin, Housewright of Gloucester, Essex, MA was born in Ipswich, Essex, MA about 1675 and died by 1764. He was son of Samuel2 Griffin (son of Humphrey Griffin) and Lydia Younglove. He married Elizabeth York. Proof can be found in the prob
1 CONC ate records of the respective families. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Massachusetts, Probate Court (Essex County). The Probate Records of Essex County, Massachusetts. (Salem, Massachusetts: The Essex Institute, 1916, 1917, 1920)
1 CONT 313:590.
1 CONT Appointment of "his [Samuel Younglove's] grandson Sam[uel]ll Griffen of Gloster" as admin of the estate of Lydia (Younglove)(Griffen) Witham shows Samuel Griffen's mother was Lydia Younglove. See discussion in The Great Migration.
1 CONT 
1 CONT  Anderson, Robert Charles; George F. Sanborn; and Melinde Lutz Sanborn. The Great Migration: Immigrants to New England, 1634-1635. (NEHGS, 1999-2011)
1 CONT discussion pages 561-2.
1 CONT https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/great-migration-immigrants-to-new-england-1634-1635-volume-vii-t-y/image?pageName=561&volumeId=13260&rId=24793295
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Hoyt, David W. The Old Families of Salisbury and Amesbury, Massachusetts. (Providence, RI, 1897-1919), 373, 967. link to 967 Read Anderson's comments on this work and Hoyt's later work An Emerson-Benson Saga (2003) 614 in the Great Migration above.
1 CONT 
1 CONT https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=wu.89061707279;view=1up;seq=167
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT  
1 CONT Charles Francis Griffin: Grifing., in The New York Genealogical and Biographical Record. (New York, New York: New York Genealogical and Biographical Society), 55:99, Jan 1924.
1 CONT 
1 CONT  
1 CONT Anderson, Robert Charles; George F. Sanborn; and Melinde Lutz Sanborn. The Great Migration: Immigrants to New England, 1634-1635. (NEHGS, 1999-2011), 2:7:560 see discussion pages 561-2.
1 CONT 
1 CONT  
1 CONT Babson, John J. History of the town of Gloucester, Cape Ann: including the town of Rockport. (Gloucester Mass.: Procter Bros., 1860), 78.
1 CONT 
1 CONT "Our first Samuel had in 1707 two acres of land where he had set his house near Benj. York's land; and four acres on the east side of the way leading from Lobster Cove to Sandy Bay" He had sons Samuel, Adoniram and Daniel. Samuel Griffin, jun., fo
1 CONC r many years a member of the church at Annisquam, and a useful citizen, died Jan. 15, 1781;" "Samuel Griffin first appears in Gloucester on his marriage to Eliz. York Dec.15, 1703.There was a family of this name early settled in Ipswich. Humphrey m
1 CONC ay have been ancestor of Samuel and a Samuel who is said to have moved from Newbury in 1736.
1 CONT 
1 CONT  Pringle, James Robert. History of the town and city of Gloucester, Cape Ann, Massachusetts. (Gloucester, Mass.: Procter Brothers, 1860)
1 CONT 63.
1 CONT "Samuel Griffin appears in town on the occasion of his marriage to Elizabeth York, Dec. 15, 1703. He probably came from Ipswich, where Humphrey Griffin settled in 1641. Samuel had a grant of land on the road leading from Lobster Cove to Sandy Bay
1 CONC . His numerous descendants are among the active and energetic businessmen of the town."
1 CONT 
1 CONT  
1 CONT Griffin, in Davis, Walter Goodwin. The ancestry of Annis Spear, 1775-1858, of Litchfield, Maine. (Portland, Maine: Southworth-Anthoensen Press, 1945), 147.
1 CONT 
1 CONT   Samuel York, in Noyes, Sybil; Charles Thornton Libby; and Walter Goodwin Davis. Genealogical Dictionary of Maine and New Hampshire. (Portland, Maine: Southworth Press, 1928-1939).
1 CONT Samuel and Hannah York has Elizabeth York who married Samuel Griffin. They quit claimed to son Samuel Griffin Jr in 1754 citing York Deeds 30:258
1 CONT 
1 CONT werelate.org/wiki/Person:Samuel_Griffin_%2818%29
