0 @N2086@ NOTE Page 394:
1 CONT Birth of Thomas Foster, born about 1600:
1 CONT This research also notes that the immigrant Thomas Foster, born about 1600, gave the uncommon name of Hopestill to one of his sons, which most certainly denotes a close relationship with Hopestill Foster, of Dorchester, who was the son of Hopestil
1 CONC l Foster, senior.  This relationship gives indication that these Foster immigrants came from the County of Kent in England.  Thomas Foster, christened 30 Dec 1599, son of Thomas Foster in Cranbrook, Kent, England, may be the Thomas Foster, born abo
1 CONC ut 1600, who immigrated to Colonial America.
1 CONT 
1 CONT (Thomas Foster born 1599/1600 married Elizabeth ______ , born about 1618, whose maiden name is still unknown; married in about 1639 at Weymouth, Norfolk, Massachusetts Bay Colony): 
1 CONT Thomas Foster held the office of deacon [in the Church].  No record is found of his marriage; [no colonial marriage records exist before 1640, and Thomas Foster appears to have married in 1639.]; but in March 1648 and in November 1679, he had a wif
1 CONC e Elizabeth, probably the same who is provided for by his will, dated April 18, 1682, and probably also the mother of all his children.  He died April 20, 1682.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Family of Thomas Foster, page 394, bottom paragraph:  
1 CONT 1. Several persons bearing the name of Foster, but apparently of different families, are found among the early inhabitants of New-England.  One of those persons was Thomas Foster, who resided in Weymouth, [Massachusetts Colony] as early as 1640.  T
1 CONC here seems to be good reason to suppose, with Farmer and Savage, that he subsequently resided in Braintree and in Billerica ... 
1 CONT Page 395: 
1 CONT ... [Thomas Foster held] the office of deacon [in the Church].  No record is found of his marriage; [no colonial marriage records exist before 1640, and Thomas Foster appears to have married in 1639.]; but in March 1648 and in November 1679, he ha
1 CONC d a wife Elizabeth, probably the same who is provided for by his will, dated April 18, 1682, and probably also the mother of all his children.  He died April 20, 1682.  
1 CONT Their children were: 
1 CONT i. Thomas [Foster] born in Weymouth, [Norfolk, Massachusetts Colony] on 18 Aug 1640; died Sept. or Oct. 1679.
1 CONT ii. John [Foster] born in Weymouth, [Norfolk, Massachusetts Colony] on 7 Oct 1642; died 13 June 1732.
1 CONT iii. Increase [Foster] born in Weymouth, [Norfolk, Massachusetts Colony].  No trace is found of his history; the name is inserted on authority of Mr. Savage. 
1 CONT iv. Elizabeth [Foster] born in ___________; married 22 January 1666/1667 to James Frost, deacon, of Billerica, [Massachusetts Colony].  [Dual year dates are needed in the British calendar for dates prior to 1752, and between January 1 through Marc
1 CONC h 24, because the 1st day of the year changed from March 25 (LadyDay) to January 1st in 1752.] 
1 CONT v. Hopestill [Foster] born in Braintree, [Massachusetts Colony] on 26 March 1648; died 26 May 1679. 
1 CONT vi. Joseph [Foster] born in Braintree, [Massachusetts Colony] on 28 March 1650; died 12 December 1721.
1 CONT 
