0 @N2101@ NOTE Bio on Findagrave Memorial Page:
1 CONT “ He was born in Providence Plantations c.1638, and he died at Musketa Cove, Oyster Bay Twp, Long Island, NY (now Glen Cove) after Feb 15,1682/3 and before Mar 15,1683/4.
1 CONT 
1 CONT He married, first, about 1658, Hannah Carpenter. (The date of Apr 21,1659 recorded in early sources is questionable because it is the same date as the day on which Hannah's father's will was proved.)
1 CONT 
1 CONT He married, second, before Sep 2,1674, Ann Weeks/Wickes.
1 CONT Children(by first marriage: Hannah Carpenter Thornycraft, Thomasin Carpenter Williams, Joseph Carpenter Jr, William Carpenter, and Nathaniel Carpenter.
1 CONT Children(by second marriage): possibly Ann Carpenter Weeks, Benjamin Carpenter, and John Carpenter.”
