0 @N2126@ NOTE This Rebecca is not Rebecca Husted born in 1645. She would have been 11 years old when she conceived Rebecca born in 1657.
0 @N2127@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Rebecca LRWK-F9Z is the wife of Jonathan Reynolds.  KNZC-18C was assigned to Rebecca Husted, daughter of Angell Husted WHO DID NOT MARRY Jonathan Reynolds. She would have been 11 years old when Rebecca Husted was born in 1656 according to Jonatha
1 CONC n Reynold's Will.  They are not the same!!!!
1 CONT 
1 CONT Many of the sources and memories attached are the same. The children are the same. The husband is the same.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Both profiles lack factual dates. Life Sketches are changeable. There is no expert agreement on her last name or parents.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Does this Jonathan Reynolds really need 2 different Rebeccas as wife?
1 CONT 
1 CONT Again - at this moment these 2 Rebeccas are really the same person. ***
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT * Updated info;
1 CONT 
1 CONT Angell Husted's Will lists his son-in-law, Jonathan Reynolds as an administrator of his Estate in 1706. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Please do not merge KNZC-18C Rebecca Husted with Mrs. Rebecca Reynolds LRWK-F9Z. There are patrons who believe Jonathan Reynolds married Rebecca Husted born in 1645 in Greenwich, CT (father is Angell Husted) and there are patrons that believe he ma
1 CONC rried another Rebecca whose last name is unknown and who was born in 1634 in England. Some patrons believe that Mrs. Rebecca Reynolds married Angell Husted after Jonathan died, since their son, Jonathan Reynolds was co-executor for Angell's estate
1 CONC .  It is fine for Jonathan Reynolds and his children to be linked to multiple wives and mothers.
1 CONT 
1 CONT From "The Great Migration Begins":  ANGELL HUESTIS, b. say 1624; m. (1) by about 1645 _____ _____; m. (2) after 1673 Rebecca (_____) Reynolds, widow of Jonathan Reynolds [TAG 73:201-6].
1 CONT 
1 CONT  BIRTH;, PARENTS, MAIDEN SURNAME & MARRIAGE DATA FOR REBECCA, WIFE OF JONATHAN REYNOLDS AND PROBABLY 2ND WIFE OF ANGELL HUSTED/HUESTED IS UNKNOWN AND CANNOT BE VERIFIED.  See The American Genealogist, Vol. 73, No. 3, July 1998, pp. 201-206, "Rebecc
1 CONC a Revisited," by Gordon L. Remington. Remington claims that Anglell Husted's 2nd wife and widow Rebecca was probably the widow of Jonathan Reynolds, whose estate was inventoried 23 January 1673/74, and thus could have married Angell Husted as a sec
1 CONC ond wife. He named her son Jonathan Reynolds as a co-administrator of his estate (along with his son, Samuel Husted) to see that Rebecca's rights were fairly represented. None of this has been proven, but Remington thinks that this could be true.
1 CONT 
1 CONT *There is no marriage record for the Jonathan Reynolds who died around 1673, but the probate record for that Jonathan Reynolds does still exist, and a copy of it can be found on file in the  Fairfield, Connecticut Probate Records. It records he die
1 CONC d intestate. It includes the name of his spouse, Rebecca, and states in the will that she was the daughter of Angell Husted. It also includes his children and the name of the person in charge of his estate, Joseph Mead. It's unknown whether Gordo
1 CONC n Remington ever saw what is left of the actual will or not. Mr. Remington has also never provided any documented proof of who Rebecca was, he was simply guessing. Gordon Remington made a huge error with other colonial ancestors of mine, and it too
1 CONC k decades before documents were found to prove him wrong. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Please also bear in mind that these people lived in a small community and families intermarried and gave their children the same first names for generations. There were several Jonathan Reynolds, John Reynolds, Rebecca Reynolds and Rebecca Husted's
1 CONC , all living in the same area during the same time period.
