0 @N2271@ NOTE Find a Grave Memorial ID: 64231893.
0 @N2272@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT According to the book, Genealogy of the Fairbanks Family in America, 1633-1897 (see Sources), Mary was born in England and came with her family to Massachusetts Bay with her father Jonathan and mother Grace. The family eventually settled in Dedha
1 CONC m with six children - John, George, Mary, Susan, Jonas, and Jonathan, all who were born in England. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Settled in 1635 by people largely from Roxbury and Watertown, Dedham was incorporated in 1636. At the first public meeting on August 15, 1636, eighteen men signed the town covenant. Mary's father was not one of the first eighteen, but reportedly si
1 CONC gned not long after in September with his oldest three sons. It is thought that Jonathan came to Massachusetts Bay about 1633, settling first in Boston, but by about 1636 had removed to Dedham. The home Jonathan built in Dedham known as the "Fairba
1 CONC nk House" is today the oldest surviving wood framed house in North America.  It was built around 1637 and I think that Mary likely lived there until her first marriage in 1644.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT According to this same book, Mary was born in 1622, but the birth dates of the other siblings were unknown to the author at the time the book was published, but have since been proven. Mary's birth is given in The Genealogy of the Fairbanks Famil
1 CONC y on page 31 as "born Apr. 18, 1622."  I literally have no idea how the author may have known a birthdate, since only christening records were kept in England.  There is no way this is accurate.  Luckily, the information in The Genealogy of the Fai
1 CONC rbanks Family has been updated.  See the article by Ruth Fairbanks Joseph and James Swan Landberg, "Jonathan Fairbank of Dedham, Massachusetts, and his family in the West Riding of Yorkshire," NEHGR Vol. 166 (July 2012), p. 165, where the authors p
1 CONC ublish the actual christening records for Jonathan and Grace's children.  I have also attached an original christening record below from February 1621/2.   
1 CONT 
1 CONT So besides her original christening record, the next record we find Mary's name in is from her marriage to Michael Metcalf. See record attached below.  They had five known children, all born in Dedham, all with birth records in Dedham:  
1 CONT 1.  Michael
1 CONT 2. Mary
1 CONT 3. Sarah
1 CONT 4. Jonathan
1 CONT 5. Eliaser 
1 CONT Unfortunately Michael died in 1654 and left behind a family of small children.  It is likely that he died suddenly, as I don't believe he left behind a will.  However, his son Michael was remembered in the will of his father of the same name.  Se
1 CONC e Metcalf Genealogy attached below, page 19.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT It looks like Michael died 24 December 1654.  Her marriage record to Christopher Smith appears to be from 2 August 1654.  I believe one of the other of those dates to be slightly off, as she clearly did not marry again before her first husband died
1 CONC .  
1 CONT Regardless, Mary married Christopher Smith about 1654 and they had one known children together.  See birth record for John Smith below.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT Mary's father Jonathan died in 1668 and his will was executed the same year. His moveable estate went to his wife Grace, and bequests were made to his children, including his second son George, his daughter Mary wife of Christopher Smith, Jonas, Jo
1 CONC nathan, Sarah (eldest daughter of his son John), and to Susan's son Ralph Daye. His estate went to oldest son John, who was made sole executor of the will. John married Sarah Fiske and remained in Dedham on the estate.  Specifically related to Mar
1 CONC y his will stated: 
1 CONT "And I giue & bequeath to my daughter Mary the wife of Christopher Smith the sume of sixteene pounds, which sixteene pounds I glue to my said daughter in prticuler, And distinct from her husbans Estate & to be allwayes at her dispose, this sixtee
1 CONC n pounds to be payed in two equall (sum'es ?) of Eight pounds."
1 CONT Not long after her father's death, Mary's second husband Christopher died in 1676.  From his findagrave file: 
1 CONT "Christopher Smith d. intestate Nov. 7, 1676 at Dedham, Mass. His widow Mary was appointed administratrix, with their son John Smith along with Daniel Fisher, all of Dedham, giving a bond for 410 pounds. The inventory of his estate dated Dec. 13, 1
1 CONC 676 includes numerous farm animals, 19 acres of meadow, 5 acres of upland planting field, 1 lot in the great plain, 12 acres in the upland pond field, and 27 acres at what later became Natick, Mass."
1 CONT 
1 CONT Mary remained a widow for 8 years before she died in 1684. See source attached below.  She left behind a will.  Someone has scanned the will in under the Memories tab.   It mentions: 
1 CONT 1.  Her son Michael Metcalfe
1 CONT 2.  Her brother John Fairbank
1 CONT 3.  Her son John Smith
1 CONT 4.  Her daughter Sarah Wares, wife of Robert Wares
1 CONT 5.  Her daughter Hannah Meatcalfe.  I think she was referring to her daughter-in-law, Jonathan's wife
1 CONT 6.  Her daughter Melatia Meatcalfe.  I think she was referring to her daughter-in-law, Eleazer's wife
1 CONT 7.  Her son Jonathan Meatcalfe
1 CONT 8.  Her son Eleazer Meatcalfe
1 CONT 9.  Her daughter Mary Wares.  Mary had also married a Ware - John Ware.  She also mentioned Mary's two sons, John and Eleazer Wares.  
1 CONT Mary has no headstone and any final resting place for her would need to be considered speculative. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT ------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT From Mary's find-a-grave file:  
1 CONT Mary Fairbanks, eldest dau. of Jonathan Fairbanks, Sr. and Grace Smith. She d. testate June 4, 1684 at Dedham, Mass.
1 CONT On Apr. 2, 1644 at Dedham, Mass., Mary m. 1) Michael Metcalf, Jr., b. or bapt. Aug. 29, 1620 at Norwich, England, s. of Michael Metcalf, Sr. and Sarah Ellwyn. Five children were born of this marriage. Michael d. Mar. 25, 1654 at Dedham and Mary m
1 CONC . 2) Aug. 2, 1654 at Dedham, Mass., Christopher Smith, who. d. Nov. 7, 1676 at Dedham. There was one child of this second marriage. 
1 CONT The Fairbanks Genealogy (1897) offers two dates of death for Mary (Fairbanks)(Metcalf) Smith: "10. 3. 1676 or 4: 4: 1684." The second date of death (June 4, 1684) is of Mary nee Fairbanks, being "Mary Smith, widdow" (DeVR, 20.) The earlier date (Ma
1 CONC y 10, 1674) is for Mary, first wife of Asahel Smith of Dedham (DeVR, 15.) See Asahael Smith in the Dedham Historical Register, Vol. 8, April 1897, pp. 38-42 and July 1897, pp. 95-6.
1 CONT The will of Mary (Fairbanks) (Metcalf) Smith of Dedham, relict of Christopher Smith dec'd, is dated May 30, 1684. The inventory of her estate was taken July 11, 1784. In the will she remembered son John Smith (by her 2nd husb.) and the children b
1 CONC y her 1st husband: sons Jonathan and Eleazer Metcalf; daus. Melatiah (Metcalf) Metcalf, Sarah (Metcalf) Ware; two sons of her dec'd dau. Mary (Metcalf) Ware; dau.-in-law Hannah, wife of son Jonathan Metcalf, Jr.; and her brother John Fairbanks. (Su
1 CONC ffolk, Mass. PR #1360).  
1 CONT -------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT In the attached records below regarding her marriage to Christoher Smith and the birth of her son John, there seems to be some confusion about whether her name was Mary or Martha.  Since Mary is referred to in her father's will as the wife of Chris
1 CONC topher Smith, and since her own will mentions sons from both marriages, it seems that any reference to her as "Martha" may be in error.
