0 @N2277@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Please note that the Family Data Collection is not based on ANY primary sources, and dates on Find-a-grave can be created without any actual gravestone to document those dates.  The birth year on www.FindAGrave.com is estimated at 1686, but that i
1 CONC s two years after her father's death.  The birth year in FDC shows 1670 for Sarah; however, we show that she was having children as late as 1724, which would have been far too old for a woman in the 1700s.  Likewise, the marriage date claimed on Fa
1 CONC mily Data Collection is 1686, which is unlikely if her first child was not born until 1706 -- that's 20 years of being infertile after marriage, only to have seven children into her 40s to 50s.  Therefore, please stop to evaluate these dates show
1 CONC n in unsupported records and realize that they are most likely erroneous.
1 CONT 
1 CONT ** Note I agree with the above statement but am spelling out a website that has been shortened to a term offensive to some. To the author- no disrespect intended and nothing else has been altered.
