0 @N2437@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Son of George Alcock and Ann Hooker Alcock.
1 CONT 
1 CONT From Wikitree:
1 CONT 
1 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Alcock-39
1 CONT 
1 CONT In1630, he emigrated with his parents to New England[1] [2]
1 CONT 
1 CONT John was a physician, who graduated from Harvard in 1646, and set up practice in Roxbury[1] [2]
1 CONT 
1 CONT About 1648, John married Sarah Palgrave, daughter of Richard Palgrave[1] [2] [3], and their children included[4] :
1 CONT 
1 CONT Joanna, who was born and died in 1649[2]
1 CONT Anna[1], baptized May 26, 1650[4], who married John Williams and Robert Guthrie[2]
1 CONT Sarah[1], baptized May 26, 1650[4], who married Zachariah Whitman, a minister who served in Hull[2]
1 CONT Mary, baptized August 16, 1652[4], who married Joshua Lamb[2]
1 CONT George[1], baptized March 25, 1655[4], who died in 1676, and named most of his siblings in his estate[2]
1 CONT John[1], baptized March 15, 1657/7[4] a merchant who died unmarried in 1690[5] [2]
1 CONT Elizabeth[1], baptized March 27, 1659[4] [2]
1 CONT Joanna[1], baptized June 6, 1660[4] [2]
1 CONT Palgrave[1], baptized August 20, 1662[4], who married Esther[2]
1 CONT Sarah (Palgrave) Alcock died November 27, 1665[6]
1 CONT 
1 CONT John died March 27, 1667[6] [7], and was buried on March 29[8] in Eustis St. Burying ground in Roxbury. No known grave marker survives. [9]. His will, dated May 18, 1666 and proved May 2, 1667, divided his estate among the children noted here[10] [
1 CONC 2]
1 CONT 
