0 @N2553@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hopkins-1658
1 CONT Biography
1 CONT Hannah was born in Roxbury,Suffolk County, Massachusetts on January 3,1656 to William Hopkins and Hannah Andrews [1]
1 CONT 
1 CONT The marriage between Phillip and Hannah turned out to be an unhappy one.  In 1684 she was excommunicated having absconded with one Mason to the West Indies. Jamaica records show that John Murray and Hannah Gosse being lawfully asked in ye parish Ch
1 CONC urch in Port Royall in ye Island aforesaid was Joined together in the holy bonds of Matrimony ye twenty-third day of March 1687. John Holland of Boston accepted a letter of Attorney from Philip to bring a child of his from Jamaica, now in the posse
1 CONC ssion of his wife. Hannah refused to give up the child saying that Philip had one child of hers, that she had as much right to him as he had, and as much money, etc. In 1692, Port Royal was hit with a large earthquake, which destroyed most of the c
1 CONC ity. (“Descendants of William Hopkins,” freepages.genealogyrootsweb.com/ ~flebbe/surnames/hopkins.html, Ap.19,2003)
1 CONT 
1 CONT It is thought that Hannah died in the devastating 1692 Jamaica earthquake. (Find a Grave)
1 CONT 
1 CONT Divorce of Hannah Hopkins (April 1690)
1 CONT "Hannah bapt in the church in Roxbury by Rev John Eliot March 6, 1660, m Philip Goss, a sailor, the son of John Goss. On April 16, 1678 Hannah Hopkins was censured in the Church with admonication for fornication with her husband before yei wrand fo
1 CONC r flying away from justice unto Road Island (Record of the Commissioners of the City of Boston). On October 9, 1678 Hannah Hopkins alias Gosse was called to confess her sins & manifest her repentance for fornication and running away to Road Island
1 CONC . She confessed and was absolved and received to take hold on the covenant (Roxbury Church Records). In 1690 Goss applied for a divorce on the grounds that she had left him and married another man in Jamaica (Early records of S.J.C. of Massachusett
1 CONC s, file 2553), to wit:
1 CONT 
1 CONT To the honorable Simon Bradstreet Esq. Gov., Thomas Davenport Esq Dep Gov. and the rest of the Honorable Magistrates Sitting in Court of Assistants at Boston April 8, 1690. The humble Petition & Motion of Philip Goss humbly showeth: That yourner ab
1 CONC out twelve or fourteen years ago was married to Hannah Hopkins, daughter of William Hopkins of Roxbury and lived with her some years, but the petitioner being a saylor, and he being away at sea, the said Hannah removed to Boston and went tnt to Jam
1 CONC aica with one Thomas Waafe, and told him her husband had sent for her to Jamaica. Mr Waafe left her there, and since that time he hath been there several times and saw said Hannah and she informed that she was married to one John Murrayy, a joyner
1 CONC , with whom she now liveth and hath a child by him said Murray borne of her body as she owned to Mr. Waafe and also to John Larkin whose evidences are now in the hands of Worshipfull Jno Phillips Esq. I have also a certificate from thhe clerke of y
1 CONC e Parish of Port Royall in Jamaica of her being marryed to said Murray. The premises being considered your petitioner humbly request the favor of this honorable Court that according to the Laws of God and this Jurisdiction he may be Divorced from s
1 CONC aid Hannah. She having broked convenant with him as may appear and your said petitioner shall as in duty bound shall ever pray. Philip Goss"[2][3]
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT ↑ "Massachusetts, Town Clerk, Vital and Town Records, 1626-2001," database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-9979-QCNC?cc=2061550&wc=Q4D4-7MS%3A353350401%2C355675801%2C355679401 : 13 July 2016), Suffolk > Rox
1 CONC bury > Births, marriages, deaths 1630-1844 > image 8 of 252; town clerk offices, Massachusetts.
1 CONT ↑ "Colonial Hopkins and Some of Their Descendants" notes by Timothy Hopkins, edited by Margaret Griffith, San Francisco, 1951, page 76. Condensed version follows:
1 CONT ↑ http://adupree.com/wp/g/familygroup.php?familyID=F922&tree=adupree
1 CONT Acknowledgements
