0 @N2555@ NOTE “...In the Rappahannock valley, in Sittenbourne parish, CAPTAIN SIMON MILLER reported about 600 pounds sterling lost to stock and property.  Simon Miller was born in Bristol, England, in 1642.  His will is dated February 16, 1679, in whic
1 CONC h he says he is “aged seven and thirty years or thereabouts.”  SIMON MILLER MARRIED MARGARET PROSSER, WIDOW OF JOHN PROSSER. “
0 @N2556@ NOTE IN THE NAME OF GOD AMEN. I JOHN PROSSER of the GOLDEN VALLE in the Parish of Sittingbourne in the Freshes of Rappae County being very sick and weak but yet in perfect strength of memory blessed be God doe make this my last Will and Testamen
1 CONC t in manner and forme following
1 CONT 
1 CONT Imprs I give my Soule to God that gave it who is my Creator hoping to be saved by his mercy in Jesus Christ my Savior and Redeemer and not by any Merrits of my own for I am less that the lest of all his Mercies and my Body to the Earth wth descen
1 CONC t and Christian buriall by my first wife, Martha.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Item, I give unto my wife that now is, I meane my loving wife, Margarett, five hundred acres of land on the North side of the River joyning to five hundred acres sold to Thomas Pannell to her and her heirs and assigns for ever, and one halfe of m
1 CONC y movable Estate my Debtsand funerall charge being paid; and if my movable estate will not pay my debts, then so much of my land back upon Pewmansin to be sold by her as will fully satisfie all, she I doe hereby make my full and whole executrix t
1 CONC o execute my whole Will.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Item, I give to my Eldest son, John Prosser, my Plantation called the Nutgrove, and the land thereto belonging to his and his heires for every and in case he die without issue the surviving brethern to have it divided amongst equally.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Item, I give unto my second sonne Samuel Prosser, four hundred acres of land joyning upon his brother John, to him and his heires for ever he dying without issue the land to be divided among the surviving Brethren.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Item my Plantation of the Golden Valle and the land in that neck I give to my loveing wife Margaret, during her Naturall life and then to fall to my eldest son John Prosser and his heirs forever.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Item I give to my two sons joyntly by name Roger Prosser and Anthony Prosser a devident of land containing one thousand one hundre acres lying upon Mattepony Swamp to them and their heires for ever to be divided by lott, when the eldest of them com
1 CONC e of age and they dying without issue to be equally divided betweene the surviving Brethren; yest this shall be no barrr to any of them or to hinder any one of them from selling his own proper inheritance if occasion require.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Item I give unto my sonne in law Robert Goffe and Thomas Goffe, two hundred acres of land joyntly, joyning upon my Back Line of my divident of the Golden Valley for them and their heirs forever.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Item I what land I have over and above what I have disposed of as aforesaid to be equally divided among my four sonnes by name John Prosser, Samuel Prosser, Roger Prosser, and Anthony Porsser and I leave under God all my sonnes under the protectio
1 CONC n of my loving wife Margarett, until they come one after another to the age of eighteen and to whom she shall think fitt to put them too and do hereby desire Mr James Kay to assist my said executrix in performing all my Will and Testament and where
1 CONC as I have sold some land that as yet hadth no conveyance doe hereby impower my said executrix of Mr James Kay or his or her certain Attorney to give conveyance for the same and to acknowledge it to be recorded and in confirmation of these Revoakin
1 CONC g all other wills and testaments to this my last Will and Testament. I have set to my hand and seale this 28th day of August 1673. Signed Sealed and confirmed for the Last Will and Testamt of John Prosser in the presence of us John Waight, Hugh C P
1 CONC almer
1 CONT 
1 CONT The Witnesses hereunto according to an order of Court held for Rappae County
1 CONT were sworne before us this 30th day of Jun 1677
1 CONT         ANTHONY SAVAGE
