1 CONT 
1 CONT PETER TALLMAN, of Newport, Portsmouth, Rhode Island
1 CONT d. 1706
1 CONT m. 1st Ann
1 CONT m. 2nd 1665, JOAN BRIGGS, d. 1685.
1 CONT m. 3rd. Esther
1 CONT 
1 CONT 1655, Freeman
1 CONT 1658, Dec. 18, Bought 9 acres in Portsmouth.
1 CONT 1641, Portsmouth, General Solicitor for the Colony of R.I.
1 CONT 1661-2, Commissioner
1 CONT 1662-65, Deputy
1 CONT 1663, Assembly granted him a divorce from his wife, Ann.
1 CONT 1665, July, 24. An Ante-nuptial agreement was made between him and Joan Briggs, of Taunton. SEE BOOK for details.
1 CONT 1674, June 7, Imprisoned for breaking law prohibiting the receipt of land from Indians by deeds of gift. He gave up the deeds, and was reles.
1 CONT 1675, Oct 20, Brought suit agains Rebecca Sadler, wife of Thomas for breach of peace and threatening his family.
1 CONT 1683, Sept 18, On jury at Portsmouth.
1 CONT 1708, Inventory was presented by son, James.
1 CONT 1709, May 8, Administration having been given to Jonathan Tallman, ........
1 CONT 
1 CONT Children:
1 CONT I. Mary, d. 1720; m. John Pearce, b. 1617, d. 1707
1 CONT II. Elizabeth, d. May 20, 1701; m. Mar. 3, 1674, Isaac Lawton, b. Dec. 11, 1650, d. Jan 25, 1732
1 CONT III. Peter, b. Mar. 21, 1658, d. Jul 6, 1726; m. Nov 7 1683, Ann Walstone, widow, dau. of Benjamin & Jane Wright [See book for details]
1 CONT IV. Ann, m. Mar 8, 1679, Stephen Bratton, d. 1692
1 CONT V. Joseph
1 CONT VI. Susanna; m. Mr. Beckitt
1 CONT VII. ? d. 1732, m. William Wilber, d. 1738
1 CONT VIII. Jonathan, d. 1762; m. Sarah, d. 1748
1 CONT IX.  James, d. 1724, m. 1st. Mary Davol; m. 2nd Sept 14, 1701, Hannah Swain
