1 CONT " ...  our Brother Jonathan Talman of the towne of Dartmouth within the county of Bristoll did by the consent and aprobation of us all under written obtaine Letters of Administration from the town counsell of Portsmouth ... for to Administer ... [?
1 CONC ?] off and every part and parsell of his moveable estate of or any[?] belonging or aportaineing to the Eastate of our deceased ffather peter Talman senr of Portsmouth ... ... be it ffurther manifested and made knowne that we the under subscribers a
1 CONC nd children to the abovesaid Peter Talman abovesd deceased haveing receaved of and from the hands or order of out abovesaid Brother Jonathan Talman as he is and was Administrator to the abovesaid estate our equall parts and proportions of this sam
1 CONC e without ffraud ... manifest and oblidge our selves joyntly and severaly ... if any thing mater or cause action or debt should or shall lawffully apears that our said ffather Peter Talman deceased had not payd or discharged in his Lifetime we do h
1 CONC ereby oblidge our selves joyntly and severaly ... without any reservation to defend [?] indemnify and and to reimburse all Legall Judgments Awards Reservations of what nature soever according to Law    
1 CONT Witness our hands and seals in Portsmouth upon Rhode Island this third day of May [1709].  ...
