0 @N2612@ NOTE On pages 29–30 this source gives the children of the family that may be proven by record. In reference to the error perpetuated that Richard Smith md. a Sarah Folger, Frederick Kinsman Smith states on page 21: "It does not seem probable t
1 CONC hat Richard Smith was married before leaving England. It is more likely that he found his wife in New England. Sarah, and the tradition has been accepted by many that she was Sarah Folger, BUT THIS HAS NOT BEEEN CONFIRMED BY ANY RECORD NOW KNOWN AN
1 CONC D APPEARS NEGATIVE BY ACCEPTED FACTS. John Folger, first of the name in New England, is supposed to have had only one daughter, Mary, who married Peter Paine of Southhold. The Folgers were among the early settlers of Martha's Vineyard." An articl
1 CONC e published in 1990 in "The New York Genealogical and Biographical Record," volume 121, no. 1, (January 1990): 19–22, is entitled, "The Identity of Sarah, Wife of Richard (1) Smith of Smithtown, Long Island." Please see a summary of this articl
1 CONC e in the source listed above and one below.
