0 @N2621@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Anna White, daughter of mayflower passenger Resolved White and Judith Vassall (daughter of  William Vassall 1/9th owner of the Massachusetts Bay Corporation)
1 CONT 
1 CONT JOHN HAYWARD was born 20 December 1640, in Concord, Middlesex, Massachusetts, to George Hayward (1604-1671) and Martha Unknown (1631-1693.) He married Anna White, 2 June 1671, in Concord.
1 CONT 
1 CONT John Hayward died 22 November 1714, in Concord, at age 76.
1 CONT 
1 CONT ANNA WHITE was born 4 June 1649, Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusetts, to Resolved White, Mayflower passenger, (1615-1687) and Judith Vassall (1619-1670.) She married John Hayward, 2 June 1671, in Concord. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Anna White passed away 25 May 1714, in Concord, age 65.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 	Children of John Hayward and Anna White:
1 CONT 
1 CONT 1.	Mary Hayward, b. 1671.
1 CONT 2.	George Hayward was born 20 July 1673, in Concord, Middlesex, Massachusetts, to John Hayward (1640-1714) and Anna White (1649-1714.) He was the grandson of Mayflower passenger Resolved White. He married Hannah Chadwick, 17 January 1695, in Concor
1 CONC d, at 22 years of age. George Hayward died 5 July 1725, in Warren, Worchester, Massachusetts, at 51 years of age.
1 CONT 3.	Judith Hayward, b. 1675.
1 CONT 4.	Mercy Hayward, b. 1677.
1 CONT 5.	John Hayward, b. 1680.
1 CONT 6.	Hannah Hayward, b. 1682
1 CONT 7.	Sarah Hayward, b. 1689.
