0 @N2686@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Information taken from Genealogical and family history of southern New York and the Hudson River Valley, Vol 3, page 1647, by Cuyler Reynolds
1 CONT 
1 CONT In early English annuals this name CLOSE is found written Clowes and cloughes.  It was established at Langsley, near Macclesfield, England, in 1686.  The first record of this branch of the family in this country is found in the records of Fairfield
1 CONC , Ct, where William Frost, in his will dated January 6, 1644, mentions Goodman Close as having in possession a heifer belonging to Frost.  It is impossible now to determine whether the word Goodman was a baptismal name.  It was probably used in acc
1 CONC ordance with the custom of those days, instead of the present title "Mr."
1 CONT 
1 CONT Goodman Close probably died at Fairfield about 1653, leaving a widow, Elizabeth and children:  Hannah, Thomas, Joseph and Mary.  The widow subsequently married George Stuckey, and moved with her children to Stamford, Connecticut, where she died Sep
1 CONC t 4, 1656.  In the will of George Stuckey dated August 23, 1660, he mentions the children of Goodman Close.  Joseph, born about 1634, was then deceased; Hannah, born about 1632, married, June 9, 1657 to Joshua Knapp of Greenwich, and later to Joh
1 CONC n Bowers;  Mary born about 1640, married, June 25, 1668 to Samuel Holly, and was living in 1725.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT Goodman Close was born about 1600, in County York, England, and his wife Elizabeth about 1606.  They came to Fairfield, Connecticut about 1642.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Thomas, son of Goodman and Elizabeth Close, was born about 1637 and settled in Greenwich in 1661. He was one of the original patentees of the town, May 1665 and died about 1709, in which year his will, dated December 30, 1708, was probated. He wa
1 CONC s the ancestor of the familes of this name in Fairfield, Dutchess County, New York, and Worcester, Massachusetts. He Married in 1669, Sarah, daughter of Richard and Ann (Husted) Hardy. Children: Sarah, born December 10 1670; Hannah, March 12, 1672
1 CONC ; Thomas, December 16, 1674; Joseph,born November 20, 1676, Benjamin, born May 18, 1679 in Greenwich and died in March 1759; Mary, born 1682; Elizabeth, born August 1684; Ruth born November 1, 1687; John, born April 8, 1689 and Lydia, born 1690. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Glenn Close, an American actress, is a decendent
