0 @N2693@ NOTE Abigail Ufford in entry for Roger Terrill, Families of Early Milford, Connecticut
0 @N2694@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Arrival in US 1632
1 CONT 
1 CONT The daughter of THOMAS & ISABELL UFFORD and wife of Roger Terrill. Her estimated birth date comes from "The Great Migration Begins."
1 CONT 
1 CONT She predeceased her brother, Thomas, Jr. & her father. Her children are referred to in the will of Thomas, Jr. as "the children of Roger Terrill."
1 CONT --------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT "There is a book entitled 'Two Centuries of New Milford Connecticut' prepared for the bi-centennial celebration of 1907 by the historical committee by various citizens of New Milford. The section that covers Abigail was contributed by General Henr
1 CONC y Stuart Turrill starting on page 26 entitled 'The Two Abigails.'
1 CONT 'In this home, thus acquired, she lived for fifty-five years, rearing eleven children....' Not knowing exactly when she and Roger make their home in Milford, but using the 1639 date when we can establish them in Milford, that would mean she lived t
1 CONC here until c. 1694.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Abigail came from London, England to Boston, MA 16 Sept 1632 on the "Lyon" with her parents Thomas and Isabell Bryan Ufford. She was admitted to the Milford Congregational Church 3 Nov 1644 and had married Roger Terrill prior to that date. Their ch
1 CONC ildren were John, Abigail, Hannah, Samuel, Roger, Joseph, Mary, Ephraim, Thomas and Daniel. See memorial 29434063 for link to children
1 CONT 
1 CONT Roger and wife Abigail have a memorial stone on the Memorial Bridge Milford, Ct which I have taken a picture of in 1989.
0 @N2695@ NOTE Fourth Generation, John Bird, born in Litchfield, Conn., 1695, married, January 20, 1728, Mary Atwood, born April 20, 1705, daughter of Jonathan Atwood of Woodbury, Conn., born June 8, 1675, who married, November 5, 1701, Sarah Terrill, bor
1 CONC n March, 1684, daughter of Roger Terrill, one of the first settlers of Woodbury, Conn., whose wife was daughter of Thomas Ufford, who came from London, England, in the ship "Lion," to Boston, Mass., September 16, 1632, and removed with Pynchon, t
1 CONC o Springfield, Mass., in 1636, and thence to Milford, Conn.
1 CONT 
1 CONT (Jonathan Atwood, born June 8, 1675, was son of Dr. Thomas Atwood, who with his brother, Herman Atwood, came from Sanderstead, county of Surrey, England, in the ship "Abigail," from London, in 1635.)
