0 @N2716@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Joseph was the son of Joseph Benjamin and his first wife Jemima.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT That he was the son of Joseph Benjamin and his first wife Jemima can be easily demonstrated.  In 1686, both Joseph Benjamin of Barnstable and his wife Jemima signed a deed selling about 2.5 acres in Cambridge.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT See https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L9Z7-2H65?view=fullText&keywords=Jemima%20Benjamin%2CBenjamin%20Jemima&lang=en&groupId=
1 CONT 
1 CONT Jemima, the wife of Joseph Benjamin, was clearly alive in 1686. Joseph married his second wife, Sarah ____________, sometime between 1686 and his death in 1704.    None of Joseph's children belonged to the second wife Sarah.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Joseph has a birth record in Yarmouth in 1666.  Please note that this date conflicts with his age given in his father's probate documents.  The age given appears to be 30.  However, in order to be 30 years old, he would need to have been born abou
1 CONC t 1674, which is the same year his sister Marcy was born, so this can't be correct.  I think Joseph was 38 years old in 1704 when his father died.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT "Benjamins in America"  Joseph II served in 1695 under Capt. Gorum in the campaign against Indians at Pemaquid and was severely wounded and pensioned in 1700. Joseph was a blacksmith and settled in Preston, Conneticutt where he bought land.
