0 @N2757@ NOTE THOMAS PAINE
1 CONT Estham had been settled but a very few years when Thomas Paine became a resident.  He was born in England... Credible traditionary accounts... have it that he came over when a lad about ten years of age, with his father, Thomas, and married Mary Sn
1 CONC ow and settled in Eastham.  But as to the father, Thomas, beyond that he settled in Plymouth Colony, tradition is silent.  It has been supposed the father was the Thomas Paine who settled in Yarmouth...  It has also been supposed that the lad, th
1 CONC e subject of this article, was the Yarmouth Thomas, and that he removed to Eastham from that town.  Of this there is no evidence.... 
1 CONT 
1 CONT His name first appears upon the records as a constable of Eastham in 1653...  In 1670, Mr Paine became interested in purchasing land in what is now Truro... His first purchase was made of Gov. Prence of Plymouth, May 2, 1670...  By trade he seems t
1 CONC o have been a cooper and mill-wright... The land given by the town to Mr Paine for his building the mills... upon Mr Paine's death, passed into the hands of his son, Nicholas, who occupied it until his death... he returned to Eastham, to his hous
1 CONC e at Kescayogansett, where he spent, it is supposed, the remainder of his life, passing away Aug 16, 1706... 
1 CONT 
1 CONT His wife Mary, daughter of Nicholas Snow and granddaughter of Mr Stephen Hopkins.. to whom he was married in 1650, was a woman of whom much has been said... Her son, Deacon John Paine, thus gives in his diary an account of her last hours and death
1 CONC :  "On the 28th day of April, 1704, my honored mother, Mary Paine, departed this life, being suddenly taken and struck with death, she having reasonable health all day...
1 CONT 
1 CONT The will of Thomas Paine bears date May 12, 1705.  It was presented for probate Oct 2, 1706.  He mentions seven sons:  Samuel, Thomas, Elisha, John, Nicholas, James and Joseph; two daughters: Dorcas, wife of Benjamin Vickery of Hull, and Mary, wif
1 CONC e of Israel Cole....
1 CONT 
1 CONT His house at Keskokgansett stood between the cove and Fresh pond... His son Nicholas occupied it until his death, when it passed into possession of his daughter Patience, and her husband, William Norcot....
1 CONT 
1 CONT A deed of gift of meadow to his son Thomas, in his own handwriting is yet extant, bearing date 1684, and witnessed by his two sons, Nicholas and James.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Samuel Paine, the eldest son, married Patience Freeman, daughter of Major John Freeman of Eastham and granddaughter of Gov Prence, Jan31, 1687.... He was cut down by fever, Oct 13, 1712.  He left a wife and nine children....
1 CONT 
1 CONT Thomas Paine, the second son, born in 1657... He became a landholder at Pamet, now Truro.... He was justice of the peace, deacon of the church, captain of the military company, and a special justice of the court of common pleas..... He died June 23
1 CONC , 1721, in the 65th year of his age.  He was twice married, and father of fourteen children.... From his daughter Hannah, descended the late Hon. Horace Binney of Philadelphia.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Elisha Paine, the third son, married Hannah Doane, daughter of John Doane of Eastham, Jan 5, 1685.... He died Feb 7, 1736.  His wife died very aged, Dec 19 1758.  He was the father of ten children.  His sons, Elisha, Solomon ad John, were ministers
1 CONC ....
1 CONT 
1 CONT Deacon John Paine, the fourth son, settled in that part of Eastham, now Orleans.... He was twice married, and father of thirteen children.  His first wife, Benner, was daughter of Major John Freeman.  He died in 1731.  He was great-grandfather of J
1 CONC ohn Howard Paine....
1 CONT 
1 CONT Nicholas Paine, the fifth son, married Hannah Higgns, daughter of Jonathan... He died in the autumn of 1733.  He was the father of seven children.  His only son, Philip, died unmarried, April 10, 1725, aged 20 years and 5 months.  Hannah, his mothe
1 CONC r died Jan 24, 1731-2....
1 CONT 
1 CONT James Paine, the sixth son, born July 6, 1665, married Bethia, daughter of Col John Thacher of Yarmouth, April 9, 1691.  He went to Barnstable to reside in 1689... He died at Barnstable, Nov 12 1718... He had seven children.  Thomas, his only son
1 CONC , was educated at Harvard college, graduating in 1711.  He married Eunice Treat, and had Robert Treat Paine... Mr James Paine resided, at his death in... Barnstable....
1 CONT 
1 CONT Joseph Paine, the seventh and youngest son, married Patience Sparrow, daughter of Jonathan Sparrow of Eastham, May 27, 1691.  He removed from Eastham to Harwich, now Brewster, before 1700.... His wife was a granddaughter of Gov. Prence.  She marrie
1 CONC d for her second husband, John Jenkins of Barnstable in 1715; she died Oct 28, 1745.  Joseph Paine was the father of eleven children... Most of his descendants are in Maine...'
1 CONT https://bethelhistorical.org/catalog/item/1994.047.0002
