0 @N2759@ NOTE 1. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT The issue of Mr. Edmond Freeman and his wife Elizabeth were : — 
1 CONT 
1 CONT *2, I. Alice, born in England ; married Dea. William Paddy, Nov. 24, 1639.
1 CONT  
1 CONT *3. II. Edmund, b. in Eng. ; m. Rebecca Prence, April 22, 1646 ; and 2d, Margaret Perry, July 18, 1651.
1 CONT  
1 CONT *4. III. Elizabeth, b. in Eng., prob. 1625 ; m. John Ellis.
1 CONT  
1 CONT *5. IV. John, b. in Eng., prob. 1627; m. Mercy Prence, Feb. 13, 1649-50. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT *6. V. Mary, who m. Edward Perry about 1653. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT The question who was the wife of Edmond Freeman, sen., 
1 CONT has led to a variety of conjecture. It has sometimes been 
1 CONT supposed she may have been a Bennet ; but for no other 
1 CONT reason than that her daughter Elizabeth Ellis named her first- 
1 CONT born Bennet, and her son John named one of his children 
1 CONT Bennett, — occurrences that naturally suggest a possible reason 
1 CONT for the introduction of a surname for a Christian name. The 
1 CONT custom, a genealogist well understands, was not infrequent in 
1 CONT those days ; the mother's maiden name being selected for at 
1 CONT least one of the sons, or perhaps grandsons. It has been 
1 CONT conjectured also that her name was Beauchampe ; the reason 
1 CONT for which supposition is founded alone on correspondence that 
1 CONT does not necessarily imply it. Mrs. Freeman may have been 
1 CONT a sister of Beauchamp ; or B. may have married Mr. Free- 
1 CONT man's sister ; or Mrs. F. and Mrs. B. may have been sisters, 
1 CONT their maiden name still undivulged.
