0 @N2783@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Extensive and well-documented Wikitree profile:
1 CONT 
1 CONT His parents and birth location are unknown. See research notes below.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Thomas Look was a collier at the Lynn Iron Works. He settled in Massachusetts, whither he had come probably from Scotland to follow his trade at the newly established iron foundry at Lynn. The name Look is derived from the biblical Luke, and the fi
1 CONC rst settler so spelled it. It is a name found in Scotland before 1600 among the rentallers of the Archbishop of Glasgow. [*In the next century there were several opulent merchants of the name of Luke in the city of Glasgow. It is also of record tha
1 CONC t a considerable number of Scotchmen were employed at the Lynn Iron Works (Essex Antiquarian, XII, 70). A Thomas Lucke was a merchant of Penthurst, Co. Kent, in 1662 (Suff. Deeds, IV, 35).] Thomas, the collier, became one of the original ten associ
1 CONC ates of Salisbury in 1659 who purchased Nantucket, and through this transaction his son Thomas, born June 1646, removed to that island about 1670 and took up the share as a settler.[1][2]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Thomas Look was married to Sarah Miller and had a son by the name of Thomas Look in 1646.[3]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Birth
1 CONT 1621/2 Lynn, Essex, Massachusetts[4] Removed birth date of 31 Mar 1622 due to lack of sources.
1 CONT Marriage
1 CONT abt 1645/6 MA[4]
1 CONT ABT 1645 Lynn, Essex, Massachusetts
1 CONT Wife: Sarah Miller
1 CONT Wife: Sarah or Mary UNKNOWN
1 CONT Child: Thomas Looke or Look
1 CONT Child: Sara Or Sarah Looke
1 CONT Child: Jonathan Locke
1 CONT Child: Mary Looke
1 CONT Child: Elizabeth Look
1 CONT Child: Experience Look
1 CONT Thomas Locke (Look) was born circa 1622 in England. [5]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Marriage
1 CONT Thomas married Sarah Miller circa 1646 in Massachusetts . [6]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Death
1 CONT Thomas passed away in 1685 in Essex County, Massachusetts, United States of America. [7]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Research Notes
1 CONT His parents are unknown. Unsourced trees connect him to William Locke (1589-abt.1665) and Susanna Cole (abt.1598-abt.1674).
1 CONT 
1 CONT Sources
