0 @N2838@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Daughter of the first wife of Robert Coles, Mrs. Mary ____? Coles.  Anne's stepmother was also named Mary, but that Mary's surname was Mary Hawkshurst.  FOR CITATIONS OF SOURCES PLEASE READ:  Robert Charles Anderson, "Great Migration Begins," vol
1 CONC . 1, A-F, pages 435-438.  Page 435. "ORIGIN UNKNOWN." Migration: 1630; First Residence: Roxbury; removes Ipswich 1633, Salem 1635, Providence 1638, Pawtuxet, Warwick, 1653. Page 437 states: "BIRTH: By about 1605 based on approximated date of firs
1 CONC t marriage."
1 CONT Pages 437-438 state that:
1 CONT Robert Coles married 1) Mary 2) Mary Hawkshurst by 1637.  
1 CONT By his first wife Mary he had JOHN, b. about 1630; DELIVERANCE, b. say 1632; ANN b. say, 1634.  
1 CONT By Mary Hawxhurst, he had DANIEL, b. say 1637; NATHANIELl, b. 1642; ROBERT, b. say 1644; and SARAH, b. say 1646.  These are the family members that can be proved by primary source records.
1 CONT Robert Charles Anderson, "Great Migration Begins," vol. 1, A-F, page 437 states:
1 CONT DEATH: Warwick between 27 April 1655 and 25 October 1655.  (The settlement of his estate as published is dated 28 October 1654, but ROBERT COLES APPEARS TO HAVE MADE A DEED ON 27 APRIL 1655, and SON JOHN COLES SAYS [ROBERT] SIGNED AN AGREEMENT ON 2
1 CONC 5 October 1655, which  should be three days before the Town Council meeting if were on 28 October 1655 and not 1654.  Also, the deeds of confirmation made by  the widow of Robert Coles all come within a few months after October 1655.)  Various pare
1 CONC nts and birthplaces assigned to Robert Coles in the past suggest a wide variety of choices of persons of such name and age found in England, but there would need to be a will or other primary document that confirmed that it referred to this Rober
1 CONC t Cole or Coles of New England
