0 @N2857@ NOTE John Parks born abt. 1644 in Ulster Ireland or England.  He was son of Sir Thomas De Parke.  John migrated to Virginia in 1658.  Some state he came from Ulster, Ireland.  The Parke, Park, Parks, Parkes family is a large one.  Some members a
1 CONC dhere to the spelling Parkes while others have dropped the "e".and some the "s" and some have dropped both.  Note: Old Rappahonnock County, VA 1667- 1761 divided into Essex and Richmond count in 1692.  King George County formed from Essex County i
1 CONC n 1720 Part of the time the difference of county names does not mean a change of residence but a change in county lines. .  Spotsylvania County was taken from Essex County in 1720.  Orange County was taken from Spotsylvania Co. in 1734.  Culpeppe
1 CONC r Co was formed from Orange 
1 CONT Co in 1748.  Goochland Co was taken from Henrico Co. in 1727. Albermale Co was formed from Goochland Co. and Louisa County in 1744.  Children of John Parks and unknown wife were George Parks, Henry Parks, Robet Parks, John Parks III and Thomas Park
1 CONC s 1 born 1670 in Old Rappahanock VA died Dec 1761 in Albmarl Co. VA.  Married Sarah Miller abt 1705 in Virginia.
