0 @N2912@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Very little is known about Hannah.  We believe she was the second wife of Roger Billings.  His first wife is mentioned in daughter Mary's birth record, but there is no mention of Mary's death.  The church in Dorchester started keeping records in 16
1 CONC 36 and can be found in the book, "Records of the First Church at Dorchester ... 1636-1734" which can be found online here: https://archive.org/stream/recordsoffirstch00firs#page/154/mode/2up.  Hannah was admitted to the Dorchester church October 14
1 CONC , 1655 (page 20, her name was spelled "Hannah Billinge").  It is believed that Hannah became Roger's second wife sometime, perhaps shortly, before this time in 1655.  They had at least 4 children together: 
1 CONT 1.  Ebenezer, christened Jan. 11, 1655/6 (see page 167) "Ebinezer Billindge"
1 CONT 2. Roger, who has both a birth record and a christening record (born Nov. 18 1657, bapt. Dec. 13 1657, see page 168) "Rodger ye sone of Rodger"
1 CONT 3. Elizabeth, who has both a birth record and a christening record (born Oct. 27 1659, bapt. Nov. 27 1659, see page 170) "Elizabeth ye daughter of Rodger Belleng"
1 CONT 4. Zipporah, who has both a birth record and a christening record (born May 21 1662, bapt. June 22 1662, see page 172). Her mother Hannah died at her birth. "Zipporah ye daughter of Roger Belleng was baptized ye 22 (4) 62 being about a month old: a
1 CONC t ye birth of whom her mother dyed"
1 CONT Christening records can be found in the Dorchester church records mentioned above.  Town vital records can be found in the collection, "A Report of the Record Commissioners of the City of Boston Containing Dorchester Births, Marriages, and Deaths t
1 CONC o the End of 1815," which can be found online here: https://archive.org/details/dorchesterbirths01dorc.  Rodger is on page 5, Elizabeth on page 7, and Zipporah on page 8.   Hannah's death is also listed in these town records as "Hannah Billing Dece
1 CONC ased the 25 (3) 1662."
