0 @N2917@ NOTE Philip Goss
1 CONT Birth: 1651
1 CONT Boston
1 CONT Suffolk County
1 CONT Massachusetts, USA
1 CONT Death: May, 1698
1 CONT 
1 CONT Year of Birth Source: "Early Families of Lancaster, MA" by Rev Frederick Weiss. (Date submitted by Sheila Dunn of
1 CONT Puyallup, Washington)
1 CONT A bit of info to bring this memorial up-to-date
1 CONT Philip Goss was born in Roxbury, Suffolk, Massachusetts
1 CONT He was a sailor and a merchant by trade.
1 CONT No marriage record to first wife Hannah Hopkins can be found but they must have been married very close to when their first child [Capt. Philip Goss Jr. 1676-1747] was born because Hannah was censured in the church for "fornication with her husban
1 CONC d before they were maryed and for flying away from Justice unto Road Island." She confessed and repented and was absolved.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Still living in Roxbury, they had two girls, one in 1679 and 1680 and both were baptized but apparently died as infants. Philip and Hannah then moved to Boston where, on October 6, 1682, Hannah gave birth to William. In 1684, Hannah left for Jamaic
1 CONC a on the sloop "Swan" and took baby William with her. Shortly thereafter, she 'married' John Murray with whom she had a child.
1 CONT 
1 CONT In 1690, Philip petitioned the court for a divorce which was granted. He attempted to get custody of William during this time but Hannah would not give the child up.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Philip married Mary Prescott on 29 Mar 1690 in Concord, Middlesex, Massachusetts.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Hannah Hopkins FAG memorial: #102010080
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Thank you.
1 CONT Let me know if you have questions.
1 CONT You can edit as you see fit if you like.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Gayle
1 CONT #47223271 
