0 @N2918@ NOTE From the book "Goss Genealogy."
0 @N2919@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Philip Goss was born in Roxbury, Suffolk, Massachusetts
1 CONT He was a sailor and a merchant by trade.
1 CONT No marriage record to first wife Hannah Hopkins can be found but they must have been married very close to when their first child [Capt. Philip Goss Jr. 1676-1747] was born because Hannah was censured in the church for "fornication with her husban
1 CONC d before they were maryed and for flying away from Justice unto Road Island." She confessed and repented and was absolved.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Still living in Roxbury, they had two girls, Hannah in 1679 and Mary in 1680 and both were baptized but apparently died as infants. Philip and Hannah then moved to Boston where, on October 6, 1682, Hannah gave birth to William. In 1684, Hannah lef
1 CONC t for Jamaica on the sloop "Swan" and took baby William with her. Shortly thereafter, she 'married' John Murray with whom she had a child.
1 CONT 
1 CONT In 1690, Philip petitioned the court for a divorce which was granted. He attempted to get custody of William during this time but Hannah would not give the child up.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Philip married Mary Prescott on 29 Mar 1690 in Concord, Middlesex, Massachusetts.
