0 @N2926@ NOTE Samuel York (the son of Richard York) was  born 1645 married Hannah ---- and died 18 Mch. 1718.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT http://dunhamwilcox.net/me/durham9.htm
1 CONT YORK.
1 CONT Samuel York born 1645, father was  Richard York. Richard was in Dover, N.H. (now Durham) in 1648. He made his will in 1672 and mentioned wife Elizabeth and several children, of whom (this one) Samuel, born 1645 married Hannah ---- and died 18 Mch
1 CONC . 1718. He purchased land in Topsham in 1670 and lived there some years five miles below the falls. He thence moved to Falmouth, and thence to Gloucester, Mass. 
1 CONT Samuel York and Hannah’s children:
1 CONT His son Benjamin, born 1680, married 7 Dec. 1704 Mary Giddings.
1 CONT Their (Benjamin and Mary) son Samuel, born 13 Oct. 1715, married, 23 Dec. 1736, Joanna Skillings in Falmouth and had children, JOANNA b. 12 Dec. 1737; SAMUEL of Durham; SARAH m. Daniel Harmon; JOSEPH of Durham married Abigail Flint (1) and Margare
1 CONC t Richards (2).
1 CONT SUSANNA m. Vincent Roberts; DEBORAH m. George Copson Roberts of Cape Elizabeth.
0 @N2927@ NOTE standard
0 @N2928@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT 
1 CONT Samuel lived in Topsham, Cape Porpoise and Falmouth, Maine. He was driven by the Indians to Gloucester. He and his wife had ten children.[2] 
1 CONT The first Samuel York was seen in Gloucester was in 1695 at the birth of his son, John, by wife Hannah. John died in 1699 as did another son, Thomas. [3] 
1 CONT Samuel York died March 17, 1718, at age 73 at Gloucester. A Mrs. York died November 28, 1724, at age 70 at Gloucester as well.[2] Samuel mentioned in his will sons Samuel, Benjamin and Richard, as well as three married daughters.[3] 
1 CONT Will 
