0 @N2972@ NOTE George Proctor [II] bought land on 22 October 1690, so he probably was at least 21 years old by that date.
1 CONT Parents could not have married until 1664, after the death of Elizabeth's second husband, William Marriott; therefore George was born after 1664.
0 @N2973@ NOTE George Proctor wrote his will on 23 March 1731 (current calendar) and it was proved in court on 7 August 1738.  He was also described as deceased in a deed transaction recorded by his daughter Elizabeth and her husband, George Home, on 2 Ma
1 CONC rch 1735, so he was deceased before that date..
0 @N2974@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT George Proctor wrote his will on 23 March 1731 (current calendar), and it was proved in court on 7 August 1738.  He named his wife, Mary, and his children:
1 CONT (1)  George
1 CONT (2)  John
1 CONT (3)  Margaret
1 CONT (4)  Mary
1 CONT (5)  Elizabeth.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Note that George was married twice, first to Katherine Frank (marriage record for 1694), and secondly to a Mary, who is named in the will and was identified as an executor of the will in 1738.  Mary is also mentioned in a 1729 land transaction, ack
1 CONC nowledging her dower rights; therefore, she and George were married by that date.
