0 @N3113@ NOTE William Cash was born about 1653 and died about 708 in Westmoreland County Virginia. He married Rebeckah Maris and Elizabeth (Possibly Skinner)
1 CONT 
1 CONT Westmoreland County lies along the Potomac River and was the birthplace of George Washington. William Cash who died in 1708, Westmoreland County Virginia Is the progenitor of Cash line under discussion here. A British tax record in 1677 list Willia
1 CONC m Cash as "seated" in Washington Parish, Westmoreland County Virginia He left a will, written 16 February 1708/7, and recorded in Westmoreland Co, 25 August 1708, naming his children: William, Thomas, John, James, Howard, Joseph, Peter, and a daugh
1 CONC ter, Anise Cash. His wife, Elizabeth was named as executrix and guardian of his children, William, Thomas, Anish, until they became of age. Therefore it is believed all the other children were older than these three whose ages were given in the wil
1 CONC l. Peter Skinner was named as executor, and John Skinner a witness. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Children of WILLIAM CASH and ELIZABETH are:
1 CONT i. JOHN HOWARD CASH, b.Abt. 1677.d.25 Sept 1729 Stafford, VIRGINIA
1 CONT ii. JOSEPH CASH, b.Abt. 1686.d.1780. Virginia.
1 CONT m. (1)SUSANNAH MASON b. ? d. 1749.
1 CONT (2) Elizabeth Bryant
1 CONT 
1 CONT iii. WILLIAM CASH , JR., b. Mar 05, 1688/89.d. Apr 2, 1720.Stafford Co, Virginia Death date from Register of St. Paul's Parish, Stafford County Virginia He married ANN MOSES. William Cash, Jr. left a will in Will Bk K:19,index only. Will Bk is miss
1 CONC ing. An inventory of his estate was held in Stafford County in 1721. 
1 CONT iv. ANISH NANCEY CASH, b.Jul 31, 1693. d.1787?
1 CONT v. THOMAS CASH, b.Aug 02, 1697. d.Abt 1787
1 CONT m . Nancy Thompson
1 CONT 2. vi. ROBERT HOWARD CASH, SR. b.Abt 1703 d.Abt 1772
1 CONT 
1 CONT vii. PETER CASH, b. Abt. 1708.d.1760. Strafford County Virginia USA
1 CONT m. CHARITY BUSH b. Nov 3 1728.
1 CONT viii. JAMES CASH
1 CONT m . (1) SARAH
1 CONT (2) SARAH
1 CONT 
1 CONT WILL OF WILLIAM CASH, WESTMORELAND COUNTY, VIRGINIA.
1 CONT 
1 CONT [Wills Book 4:141-142]
1 CONT 
1 CONT In the name of God Amen! I, WILLIAM CASH, being sick and weak of body but of perfect sense and memory praise be God, do make and ordain this my Last Will and Testament Revoking all other wills heretofore made save only this in manner and form follo
1 CONC weth: I give my soul to God which gave it and my body to the Earth there to be decently buried according to the discretion of my executor in sure and certain hopes of Resurrection and that I shall see my Savior at the last day. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Item. I do make my loving wife ELIZABETH CASH my Executrix and PETER SKINNER my Executor. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Item. I give unto my loving wife my plantation with a third part of my land during her life. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Item. I give one hundred acres of land being at the head of my land westward from my plantation to my son WILL: CASH and to him and his heirs and if he dieth without male heirs then tis my will that my son THOMAS CASH shall have it and his male hei
1 CONC rs, and if my son THOMAS CASH dieth without male heirs then it is my will that it should fall to my son JOHN CASH and to his male heirs. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Item. I give the remaining part of my land, it being one hundred twenty four acres to my son JAMES CASH and to his male heirs and if he die without male heirs, then it is my will that my son HOWARD CASH shall have it and if he dieth without male he
1 CONC irs, it is my will it should fall to my son JOSEPH CASH and his male heirs, and if he dieth without male heirs it is my will that my son PETER CASH and to him and his heirs forever. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Item. I give all my personal to my loving wife after my debts is paid. In witness where of I have set my hand and seal this sixteenth day of Febr'y 1708/7. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT To my son WILLIAM CASH underlined between the seventeen & eighteen lines before signed. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT WILL: CASH sig.
1 CONT (seal)
1 CONT 
1 CONT Testes: JOHN SKINNER, JNO. THOMAS, MARY HORTON
1 CONT 
1 CONT I having a fatherly care of my children do order them my son WILLIAM CASH to live dutifully with his mother until he be of age of one and twenty and likewise my son THOMAS CASH and my daughter ANIS CASH until she be eighteen years Of age and if sh
1 CONC e or either of them will not be governed by their mother then it is my desire that my friend and Executor PETER SKINNER shall have full power over them or either of them that will not be obedient unto their mother to take them to himself for the fu
1 CONC ll time aforesaid. In witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand and seal. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT WILL: CASH sig. WILLIAM CASH age 19 yrs. 5th day of March 1708/7, THOMAS CASH age 11, 2nd day of August 1708, ANISH CASH aged 15, 31st day of July 1708. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Testes: JOHN SKINNER, JOHN THOMAS his mark.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Westmoreland County Virginia At a Court held for the said County the Last Will and Testament of WILLIAM CASH was proved by the oathes of the witnesses thereunto as also the codicil above written and ordered to be recorded 25th August 1708. 
1 CONT Recorded 30 August Test: JA: WESTCOMB, Clerk
