0 @N3247@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Excerpt from Anderson's Great Migration Study of Thomas French, Jr. IN MEMORIES
1 CONT ORIGIN: Assington, Suffolk
1 CONT MIGRATION: 1632
1 CONT FIRST RESIDENCE: Boston
1 CONT REMOVES: Ipswich 1635
1 CONT OCCUPATION: Tailor
1 CONT Appointed ensign at Ipswich 18 May 1664 [MBCR 4:2:1 06].
1 CONT BIRTH: Baptized Assington, Suffolk, 27 November 1608, son of
1 CONT Thomas and Susan (Riddlesdale) French [Dudley Wildes Anc 64].
1 CONT DEATH: Ipswich 8 August 1680.
1 CONT MARRIAGE: By 1632 Mary ___; she died at Ipswich 6 May ,1681.
1 CONT CHILDREN:
1 CONT 
1 CONT iii. JOHN, b. about 1635 (deposed aged "about forty-eight" about March 1682 [EQC 8:329] unless this is someone else); m. by 1657 Phebe Keyes (son Thomas born Ipswich 25 May 1657), daughter of ROBERT KEYES.
1 CONT 
1 CONT ASSOCIATIONS: Thomas French and his sister Alice had arrived in New England by 1632, .and their two next younger sisters, Dorcas and Susan, came in 1633. Their parents and younger siblings sailed for New England after 1633, and are not included i
1 CONC n this phase of the study. [See
1 CONT Parker-Ruggles 412-29, Dudley Wildes·Anc 63~64 and NEHGR 142:250- 52, 143:213-20, 363-64 for the ancestry of this group of French siblings.] Alice married THOMAS HOWLETT and Dorcas married first CHRISTOPHER PEAKE and then GRIFFIN CRAFTS (sketche
1 CONC s for these families will be found elsewhere in this work). Susan may have been a servant in the household of John Winthrop Jr. for a time, but otherwise left no record in New England.
1 CONT **************
1 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/French-690
1 CONT John French
1 CONT Born about 1635 in Ipswich, Essex, Massachusetts [uncertain]
1 CONT ANCESTORS 
1 CONT Son of Thomas French and Mary (Unknown) French
1 CONT Brother of Mary French, Thomas French and Mary (French) Smith
1 CONT Husband of Phebe (Keyes) French — married before 28 Feb 1659 in Ipswich, Essex, MA
1 CONT DESCENDANTS 
1 CONT Father of Mary (French) Pearson, Sarah (French) Towne, Phebe (French) Gould, Martha French, John French, Lydia French, Richard French, Hepzibah (French) Shapley and Patience (French) Fairman
1 CONT Died before Aug 1707 before about age 72 in Topsfield, Essex, Massachusetts
1 CONT 
1 CONT Biography
1 CONT Birth about 1635 -- of Ipswich, Essex, Massachusetts
1 CONT 
1 CONT John and Phebe Keyes (b. 17 Jun 1639 in Watertown to Robert and Sarah Keyes) wed sometime before 1664.[1] The couple had several children, including Mary French, Sarah French (b. 1 Mar 1664/5), Phebe French (b. 8 May 1667), Martha French (b. 9 Au
1 CONC g 1669, unmarried and living as of 1707), John French Jr. (b. 26 Aug 1671), Lidiah French (b. 17 May 1674), Richard French (b. 18 Aug 1676), Hephzibah French (b. 2 Feb 1678/9, recorded as Phebea), and Patience French (b. 23 Aug 1681).[1]
1 CONT 
1 CONT John was a tailor by trade, but also served the town of Topsfield, Massachusetts as a surveyor of highways and fences, tythingman, grandjury man, and commissioner of special errands.[1] He took the town oath of allegiance and fidelity on December 1
1 CONC 8, 1679.[1] It appears that John also served in the military as a clerk, attaining at least the rank of corporal.[1] John deeded his Topsfield homestead to John French Jr. on December 2, 1701.[1]
1 CONT 
1 CONT John passed away in about 1707.[1]
1 CONT Sources
1 CONT 1. ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 1.3 1.4 1.5 1.6 Carrie C. Edgett, George Francis Dow, ed., The Historical Collections of the Topsfield Historical Society, Volume 13, pp. 153-161 (Merrill Press, Copefield 1908). Copy available at https://archive.org/details/hist
