0 @N3251@ NOTE https://books.google.com/books?id=vWINAQAAIAAJ&pg=PA156&lpg=PA156#v=onepage&q&f=false
1 CONT 
1 CONT Page 156-7
1 CONT John French's wife was Phebe. Although no record of their marriage has been found, she was without doubt Phebe, daughter of Robert and Sarah Keys, born in Watertown, June 17, 1639. Robert Keys removed to Newbury, and died there July 16, 1647. His w
1 CONC idow married Sergeant John Gage of Ipswich, Nov. 7, 1658 and died a widow July 7, 1680 (History of Newbury) or July 7, 1681 according to the settlement of her estate.....
1 CONT 
1 CONT John French and his wife were both members of the church in Topsfield, in a list dated 1684.  There are two entries of her death:  "John French his wife drown herself may 13, 1701,"  "Phebe French dyed on ye 14th of may 1701."  There is no record o
1 CONC f his death, but it probably was between March 5, 1705/6 (the last mention of John French Jun" on town records). and Jan. 25, 1706/7 (date of daughter Mary's power of attorney, see below [2].
