0 @N3304@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Robert Spurr (1611-1703) was born in England and died in Dorchester, Massachusetts. He and Anne (ca. 1624-1712), his wife, had seven children in Dorchcester. Their sixth child, Thomas (1661-1738) and his son Thomas (1687-1767) spent their lives i
1 CONC n Massachusetts. Michael Spurr (1723-1774), son of Thomas (1687-1767) and Elizabeth Kingsley, was born in Stoughton, Mass. and died at Round Hill, Annapolis County, Nova Scotia. Michael married Jane Shippee in Stoughton, Mass in 1746. In 1760, th
1 CONC e family of eight (three boys and three girls) migrated to Annapolis County, N.S. where four more children came to the family. Michael, Jane and their descendants remained in Canada and include Spurr, Barteaux, Harris, Hennigar, Lent, Potter, Rice
1 CONC , Vroom and related families.
1 CONT Contents: v.1. Ancestry of Michael Spurr in England, Michael and Jane (Shippee) Spurr, Thomas and Eleanor (Spurr) Shed, Abraham and Mary (Lecain) Spurr -- v. 2. William and Anne (Spurr) Berteaux , Shippy Altje (Van Voorheis) Spurr, Michael and Diad
1 CONC ama (Morse) Spurr/Anna (Rice) Spurr -- v. 3. John and Abigail (Spurr) Harris, Thomas and Mary (Hood) Spurr, Jacob and Elizabeth (Spurr) Fritz, Abraham and Eleanor (Spurr) Lent.
1 CONT 
1 CONT findagrave.com   Memorial #:   111436300     Created by:  JudiT
1 CONT Robert Spurr
1 CONT Birth:  1610, England
1 CONT Death:  Aug. 16, 1703, Dorchester, Suffolk County, Massachusetts, USA
1 CONT Robert Spurr sailed on the ship Paul of London, bound for St Christophers, embarking from Gravesend, England on April 3, 1635. He settled in Dorchester in 1658.
1 CONT He married Ann (MNU) and they had children:
1 CONT Elizabeth, b Dec 4, 1658
1 CONT Lieut Robert, b Feb 12, 1661 - Jan 16, 1738
1 CONT Patience, b May 27, 1624
1 CONT Mary
1 CONT Waitstill
1 CONT John
1 CONT Info per A history of Otisfield, Cumberland County, Maine from the original grant to the close of the year 1944; It also indicates that Robert, his son Col Robert and his grandson Capt Robert are mentioned in the History of Dorchester.
1 CONT Spouse:
1 CONT   Ann Spurr (1620 - 1712)*
1 CONT Children:
1 CONT   Waitstill Spur (____ - 1732)*
1 CONT   Mary Spurr Crehore (1645 - 1697)*
1 CONT Burial:
1 CONT Dorchester North Burying Ground, Dorchester, Suffolk County, Massachusetts, USA
