0 @N3389@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Jonathan Fairbanks, LYCV-ZNQ
1 CONT The book, Genealogy of the Fairbanks Family in America, 1633-1897 by Lorenzo Sayles Fairbanks was published in 1897 and was for many years the definitive source for information on the immigrant Jonathan Fairbanks and many of his descendants.  In 20
1 CONC 12, an excellent article was published regarding Jonathan and his wife and his English origin, providing details regarding Jonathan's life in England which were unknown to Lorenzo back in 1897.  Let's look at these sources.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT According to Genealogy of the Fairbanks Family in America, Jonathan "came from Sowerby in the West Riding of Yorkshire, England, to Boston, Mass., in the year 1633, and in 1636 settled in Dedham, Mass., where he built the noted "Old Fairbanks House
1 CONC ..." The author gives no proof for the immigration year of 1633.  He author also indicates that, while he knew of 6 children of Jonathan and Grace, he had no birth information for any of them except perhaps Mary.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT The town of Dedham was established and named in 1636, and a covenant was drawn up and eventually signed by 125 men, starting in 1636.  It appears that Jonathan was a signer in 1637, followed by several of his sons.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT Jonathan apparently received, before 1637, a lot from the town and then in 1637 an additional four acres.  Thereafter, he was granted several more plots of land over many years.  See attached under Souces.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT It seems that he initial reluctance to join with the church in Dedham was overcome in 1646 "gladly received."  See attached under Sources.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT Jonathan left behind a will dated 1 June 1668 which is indexed in its entirely on pages 33 and 34.  He died 5 December 1668.  He has no existing headstone.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT Jonathan's wife was identified on page 31 as "Grace Lee," no source, no explanation.  
1 CONT -----------------------------------
1 CONT Now let's fast forward 115 years and look at the article by Joseph, Ruth Fairbanks and Landberg, James Swan. "Jonathan Fairbank of Dedham, Massachusetts, and his family in the West Riding of Yorkshire, The New England Historical & Genealogical Regi
1 CONC ster, (New England Historic Genealogical Society, Boston, Mass.) July 2012, Vol. 166, Pages 165-187. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT I couldn't find this source online, but it was heavily referenced in Jonathan's wikitree page, from which the following is quoted:   
1 CONT 
1 CONT Jonathan Fayrbanke was probably born between 1592 and 1595 in the parish of Halifax in the West Riding of Yorkshire where his father resided. His father's first wife died between 1590, when Jonathan's brother Joseph was born, and 1593 when his fath
1 CONC er remarried. Jonathan's birth was not recorded, so it is unknown which woman was his mother. If it was his father's first wife, Jonathan was perhaps born about 1592, or by 1595 if John's second wife, Isabella, was his mother.
1 CONT 
1 CONT There is no record yet found of Jonathan's baptism, though three documents, taken together, provide evidence that he was the son of John Fairbank of Thornton in Craven, a parish about 18 miles from the town of Halifax. These three documents taken t
1 CONC ogether provide the basis for believing that John Fairbank of Thornton in Craven was the father of Jonathan Fairbank of Dedham. It was first proposed in Hiram Francis Fairbanks' article, "Ancestry of Jonathan Fairbanks," printed in the 1971 reprin
1 CONC t of Fairbanks Family in America that John Fairbank of Thornton in Craven, the 1625 testator, was Jonathan's father.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Jonathan married Grace Smith [not Grace Lee] on 20 May 1617 in Halifax. Four of their six children's baptisms are recorded in Halifax between 1618 and 1625, in Warley and Shelf, areas in Halifax. 
1 CONT   
1 CONT Jonathan and Grace (Smith) Fairbank(s) had six known children, all b. at one of several towns or villages at or near Halifax, England. At the time, the Church of England required children to be baptized at the parish where the parents were then res
1 CONC iding:
1 CONT 
1 CONT • i. John Fairbanks, bapt. Feb. 8, 1617/8, d. Nov. 13, 1684; m. Mar. 16, 1641/2 at Dedham, Mass., Sarah Fiske. who d. Nov. 26, 1683 at Dedham. Eight children of the family.
1 CONT 
1 CONT * ii. George Fairbanks, bapt. Nov 28, 1619 at Shelf near Halifax, d. Jan. 10, 1682/3 at Medfield, Mass.; m. Oct. 26, 1646 at Dedham, Mary Adams, who d. Aug. 11, 1711.
1 CONT 
1 CONT • iii. Mary Fairbanks, bapt. in Feb. 1621/2 at Shelf near Halifax, d. June 4, 1684 at Dedham, Mass.; m. 1) Apr. 2, 1644 at Dedham, Mass., Michael Metcalf, Jr., b. or bapt. Aug. 29, 1620 at Norwich, England. Five children of the family. She m. 2
1 CONC ) Aug. 2, 1654 at Dedham, Christopher Smith. They had one known child.
1 CONT 
1 CONT • iv. Jonas Fairbanks, bapt. Mar. 6, 1624/5, was killed in a massacre by the Indians Feb. 10, 1675/6 at Lancaster, Mass.; m. May 28, 1658 at Lancaster, Mass., Lydia Prescott where seven children are of record.
1 CONT 
1 CONT • v. Susan Fairbanks, bapt. Dec. 10, 1627 at Thorton-in-Craven near Halifax, d. July 8, 1659 at Dedham, Mass.; m. Oct. 12, 1647 at Dedham as his 1st wife, Sgt. Ralph Day. Five children of the family. Ralph m. 2) Nov. 15, 1659 at Dedham, Abigail C
1 CONC rafts, widow of John Ruggles, dau. of Lieut. Griffin and Alice Crafts of Roxbury, Mass.
1 CONT 
1 CONT • vi. Jonathan Fairbanks, Jr., b. circa 1630, d. Jan. 28, 1711/2 at Dedham, Mass.; m. Oct. 4, 1649 at Cambridge, Mass., Deborah Shepard, dau. of Edward Shepard and Violet Charnould, who d. Sept. 7, 1705 at Dedham. Eight children of the family.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Since we have never located a christening record for Jonathan, it is not known which of his father John's wives Jonathan belongs to.  It is believed that John had the following children with an unnamed wife: 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Children of John Fairbank and 1st wife Baptized at Halifax.
1 CONT 1. Mary Fayrbanke bpt 22 Sep 1583 (father of Sowerby) m. Deane.
1 CONT 2. John Fayrbank bp 7 Aug 1586 (father of Skircote)
1 CONT 3. George Fayrbanke bp 24 Nov 1588 (father of Skircote); d. 1650 leaving a will
1 CONT 4. Joseph Fayrbanke bp 2 Aug 1590 (father of Skircote; bur Halifax 6 Sep 1591
1 CONT 
1 CONT Jonathan Fayrbanke was probably born between 1592 and 1595.  His father's first wife died between 1590, when Jonathan's brother Joseph was born, and 1593 when his father remarried.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Jonathan is perhaps best known for his home.  The Fairbanks House in Dedham, MA is the oldest known wood structure still standing in North America. Built circa 1637 for Jonathan and Grace Fairbanks and their six children, it was home to eight gener
1 CONC ations of the Fairbanks family over the course of 268 years. The Fairbanks House is now a historic house museum and on the National Register of Historic Places.
1 CONT 
1 CONT In his will, Jonathan left his son John his home in Dedham, and also mentioned John's oldest daughter Sarah.  Also mentioned in his will was his wife Grace, his son George, his daughter Mary, wife of Christopher Smith, his son-in-law Ralph Daye an
1 CONC d the "four children the said Ralph had by my daughter Susan," son Jonas, and son Jonathan.
