1 CONC m trying to correct this family according to credible sources.  Mary Hawxhurst was 2nd wife of Robert Coles. Please read on:
1 CONT Regarding husband death:
1 CONT Robert Charles Anderson, "Great Migration Begins," vol. 1, A-F, page 437 states:
1 CONT DEATH: Warwick between 27 April 1655 and 25 October 1655.  (The settlement of his estate as published is dated 28 October 1654, but ROBERT COLES APPEARS TO HAVE MADE A DEED ON 27 APRIL 1655, and SON JOHN COLES SAYS [ROBERT] SIGNED AN AGREEMENT ON 2
1 CONC 5 October 1655, which  should be three days before the Town Council meeting if were on 28 October 1655 and not 1654.  Also, the deeds of confirmation made by  the widow of Robert Coles all come within a few months after October 1655.)
1 CONT Page 437 of "Great Migration Begins" also refers to the deed of "20 january 1655/[/6] Mary Coles of Warwick, 'widow of Robert of late deceased,' confirmed a deed wherein 'my husband before his death sold unto my son-in-law Henry Townsend a certai
1 CONC n parcel of meadow being 3 acres' [WarTR 227-28].  On 5 April 1656 the same page notes "Mary Coles widow of Robert Coles late deceased' of Warwick granted to 'my son-in-law Richard Townsend 8 acres of meadow' [War TR 278].  Henry Townsend married A
1 CONC nn Coles and Richard Townsend married Deliverance Coles who were Mary (Hawxhurst) Coles' stepdaughters.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Some old sources say Mary (Hawkshurst) Coles died in "1656" which she likely did NOT because the Great Migration Begins, v. 1, A–F, 437,  confirms by primary sources that she married Matthias Harvey after 5 April 1656 [Qar TR 278] and probably be
1 CONC fore 5 February 1656/7 [NYGBR 123:12–13].  A number of sources say THEY went to Oyster Bay, L. I.
1 CONT 
