0 @N3527@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Biography
1 CONT Jacob Davis was born about 1640, to John Davis and Alice Newman and married Elizabeth Bennett 20 January 1661, in Gloucester, Essex, Massachusetts.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Jacob, youngest son of John Davis, lived at Gloucester, Massachusetts. In 1662 he had a grant of land at the head of Long Cove, and in 1682 he with others had a grant of the stream at the head of Little River on which to set up a saw mill. On Janua
1 CONC ry 20, 1661, he married Elizabeth  Bennett. They had nine children, of whom two were sons, Jacob and Aaron. Jacob Davis (father)
1 CONT died September 2, 1685, leaving an estate consisting of house, upland and meadow, half of a sloop and four canoes, cattle, sheep and swine, farming tools, saddle and pillion, gun, cutlass and belt, etc.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Their children, all born in Gloucester, Essex, Massachusetts:
1 CONT 1.) Jacobe, Feb. 26, 1662.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 2.) John, Nov. 25, 1665. Death: Mar. 24, 1665-6.
1 CONT  
1 CONT 3.) Elizabeth, 27: 4m: 1667
1 CONT 
1 CONT 4.) Susanah, June 27, 1670.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 5.) Mary, June 3, 1676. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT 6.) Aron, Nov. 11, 1678.
1 CONT 
1 CONT 7.) John, July 17, 1681. Death: Aug. 10, 1681. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT 8.) Sarah, Dec. 2, 1685. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT 9.) Jacob died 2 September 1685 in Gloucester, Essex, Massachusetts.
1 CONT 
