0 @N3570@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Parents unknown! He was NOT the son of Francis Weekes (1590-1637) and his wife Wilmot Coffin (1595-1669).
1 CONT 
1 CONT PLEASE SEE THE SCHOLARLY "GREAT MIGRATION" BIOGRAPHY IN SOURCES and MEMORIES. Prior specific birthplace and date and parents are going beyond proven primary source records documented for this person by genealogical proof standards.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Francis was referred to as a minor in 1636 when he was one of the first settlers at Providence, Rhode Island, having been brought from Massachusetts by Richard Waterman.  He was married by 1642 to Elizabeth unknown, either at Rhode Island or Long I
1 CONC sland.  There is no primary source record that proves who he was in England. No birth records for children and 4 were christened the same day in 1647. Wife's maiden surname not known. She was not Elizabeth Luther, Father of Elizabeth Weekes, Ann Ca
1 CONC rpenter, Samuel Weekes, John Weeks, Capt. Joseph Weeks, Thomas Weekes, James Jacobus Weekes, Daniel Weekes, and Elizabeth Simpkins.
1 CONT PLEASE READ THE WikiTree argument that shows why it is impossible that Elizabeth was a a daughter of Samuel Luther. Don't always recommend WikiTree articles and this one is not accurate relative to county names, giving them to time periods before t
1 CONC hey existed, but the argument about Elizabeth Unknown not being a Luther is worth reading.
1 CONT 
1 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Unknown-337439
1 CONT 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Previous contributor wrote that she was a 
1 CONT "mayflower decendant" but there is no proof of that for Elizabeth unknown, for Francis Wickes or for the alleged father Samuel Luther. None made it into having their own life sketch in the series of Great Migration books that treat from 1620 throug
1 CONC h 1635 which means The New England Historic Genealogical Society scholars found no evidence that they were there that early, unless there has been a well documented source discovered since.
