0 @N3593@ NOTE Authored work about immigrant Richard Norman, family and descendants; few references given. A more expansive work about this family just earlier by Walter Goodwin Davis in The Ancestry of Sarah Stone (1930). A more authoritative work abou
1 CONC t Richard Norman and his children by Robert Charles Anderson appears in _The Great Migration Begins ..._ (1995). 
1 CONT 
1 CONT In this 1935 work, Raymon Meyers Tingley includes the suggestion that Richard came from Suffolk, England and was born "Richard Fryeth." The author wrote, "It is supposed that he was the Richard Fryeth, alias Norman, who Oct. 23 1603, brought suit a
1 CONC gainst his step mother and half-sister, Agnes Greenleaf, but no proof has been found."  
1 CONT 
1 CONT Great Migration Study Project (1995) concluded no origin for Richard; made no mention of such name; Walter Goodwin Davis also made no mention of the ancestry suggested by Tingley. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT About Richard Norman, "born -------; died -------," wife's name not known and no estimated date of marriage given. [GJ note, for information on these topics, see Great Migration Study Project.]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Five children as John, Richard, Susanna, William and Margaret. [GJ note, _Ancestry of Sarah Stone_ and Great Migration include no child William; both report dau. Florence.]   
1 CONT 
1 CONT Continuing information about Richard's children children, except, as above, Florence. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT About John Norman ( 1613-bef 26 Sept 1672), son of Richard. John of Marblehead and Manchester, Mass.; some children baptized at Salem. Wife "Arabella" (her maiden name not discovered) who d. 23 Nov 1679. Eight children--John, b. Aug 1637 (m. Mary R
1 CONC opes); Lydia, b. Jan 1639/40; Hannah, b. 4 Jan 1641/2; Arabella Norman, b. 14 Feb 1643/4 (m. John Baldwin); Martha Norman, bpt. 17 May 1646; Richard, bpt. 5 Oct 1651 (m. Elizabeth Bullock); Joseph, bpt 8 Sept 1653, "d. young"; Joseph, bpt. 7 Sept 1
1 CONC 656; d. 1691 (m. Mary ----). 
1 CONT 
1 CONT One of several conflicting reports about a Leach marriage is found in the text about John Norman's children. Tingley suggests marriage of John's dau. Hannah Norman to Samuel Leach.
1 CONT 
1 CONT About dau. Susanna Norman. 
1 CONT Has no birth or death dates, but reports a first marriage to Robert Lockwood of Salem, "who died -----, 1650, Fairfield, Ct."); second marriage Jeffery Ferris.
