0 @N3673@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT Elizabeth 274J-48X is likely the first child born to her parents in Massachusetts Bay.  She has no birth record, and no marriage record with John Smith.  However, she is mentioned in her father's will which was written in 1682.  At that time she wa
1 CONC s referred to as Elizabeth Bennett.  Her son from her first marriage, John Smith, was also mentioned.  For the full transcript of this section of the will, see The ancestry of Lydia Harmon, 1755-1836, wife of Joseph Waterhouse ... (attached under S
1 CONC ources).  
1 CONT 
1 CONT There are two children for John and Elizabeth lived in Salem vital records: 
1 CONT Smith, Sara, d. John, farrier, and Elizabeth, Oct. 20, 1660. CTR
1 CONT 
1 CONT Smith, Elizabeth, d. John, farrier, and Elizabeth, June 5, 1662. CTR
1 CONT A farrier is a craftsman who trims and shoes horses' hooves.  I think there was more than one John Smith iiving in the area, and John's occupation was listed as a clarification.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT There is no birth record for her son John Smith, Mary Smith, or Abraham Smith, but these children are listed in the Lydia Harmon book above.  See page 35.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT This source lists the following children for Elizabeth and her first husband John: 
1 CONT 1.  John Smith - He married Ann Skery February 6, 1689.  He was a maltster in Salem in 1692.
1 CONT 2. Mary Smith - She married Mark Haskell of Beverly, carpenter, March 20, 1677/8.
1 CONT 3. Sarah Smith - b. Oct. 20, 1660; married John Clark of Beverly, weaver.
1 CONT 4. Elizabeth Smith - b. June 5, 1662; m. Humphrey Horrill of Beverly, Jan. 10, 1687/8.
1 CONT 5. Abraham Smith - By deed and release from his brother and sisters he acquired the Goodale homestead, which had been left by his grandfather to his mohter, and also the property deeded to her in 1678.  He conveyed the estate to his son, Nathan, i
1 CONC n 1740. 
1 CONT 
1 CONT After her first husband's death, Elizabeth married, as her second husband, William Bennett.  Her marriage record can be found in Salem vital records: 
1 CONT Bennett, William, and, wid. Elizabeth Smith, Mar. ––, 1674-5.
1 CONT 
1 CONT According to Robert Charles Anderson in his Great Migration series (see attached under Sources): "this marriage record as published from the court copy gives the groom's name as "William," but in deeds he is called "Henry," and these seem to be th
1 CONC e more reliable records."  
1 CONT 
1 CONT I could understand if just the marriage record appeared to call Elizabeth's husband by the wrong first name, but that isn't the case.  William and Elizabeth are also mentioned in the birth record of their daughter Grace: 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Bennett, Grace, d. William and Elizabeth, Feb. ––, 1676. CTR
1 CONT 
1 CONT and William and Elizabeth are also mentioned in the death record for Grace: 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Bennett, Grace, d. William and Elizabeth, abt. Feb. ––, 1676. CTR
1 CONT 
1 CONT Elizabeth's husband is clearly named William in all these records.  
1 CONT 
1 CONT Written by Rachelle Child.  Please don't make changes to this Brief Life History without checking with me first.  Just common courtesy.  Thanks!
