0 @N3694@ NOTE ** NB  This author's work should not be trusted.  He makes easily avoidable mistakes (Peter's departure/arrival ship is unknown; he did not have a daughter Eleanor; & had two other children that the author was unaware of), based on someon
1 CONC e telling him about notes written by a great-grandfather.  He clearly did not use or reference primary sources to support these conclusions. **
1 CONT 
1 CONT image 3 of 24 Peter Worden came to Plymouth aboard "Anne." 5 of 24 Peter was born 1569 in Clayton, Lancashire, England and died in Yarmouth, Massachusetts in 1638. His will dated 9 Feb 1638 in Yarmouth was probated 5 March 1638/9. His heir was Pete
1 CONC r II who was born 1609 (6 of 24) His daughter, Eleanor (Ellen or Hellen) came with him aboard the "Anne." Eleanor was born 1598 and died 5 Dec 1681 in Marshfield, Massachusetts. She married 1st John Adams and 2nd Kenelm Winslow. page 3 (7 of 24). K
1 CONC enelm Winslow's son married Mercy Worden, daughter of Peter II. Page 4 gives the will (dated 2 May 1681) of his wife, Mary who died 25 March 1687. The inventory of Mary Worden was given to the judge 31 May 1687 and recorded 8 June 1687. page 5 (9 o
1 CONC f 24) gives the children of Peter II and Mary. Mercy was born 1640 and died 22 Sep 1688 and had married her cousin, Kenelm Winslow.
