1 CONT Once a resident of Longmeadow. Remains likely buried in a mass grave located at Springfield Cemetery. (see picture of memorial) "The Lost Cooley Plot"
1 CONT Ref. Elm Street Cemetery, Longmeadow, MA (1630-1830)Eliminated to make way for railway. Ref. Old Burying Yard, Springfield, MA Ref. Longmeadow Historical Society, Longmeadow, MA,
1 CONT Elizabeth was the first wife of Daniel Cooley. 
1 CONT Children(by first marriage): Benjamin Cooley, Daniel Cooley Jr, Simon Cooley, John Cooley, Thomas Cooley(husband of Rebecca Elmer Cooley Kibbe), Elizabeth Cooley Field, and William Cooley.
1 CONT 
1 CONT In 1680, on Dec. 8, Daniel Cooley married Elizabeth Wolcott. He was 29 years old, and Elizabeth was 18. She was the third generation in this country, her grandfather, Henry Wolcott, having come to America in 1630.  Her father was Simon Wolcott. He
1 CONC r Mother was Martha Pitkin, sister of Mr. William Pitkin, the progenitor of the Pitkin family in America, and of Roger Pitkin of London. She was born in England in 1638.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Source: The Cooley Genealogy
