1 CONT Samuel Griffin of Ipswich son of Humphrey and Elizabeth (____) Griffin married Lydia Younglove. Children:
1 CONT 
1 CONT Samuel Griffin b about 1675 in Ipswich (birth not recorded) of Gloucester, MA m Elizabeth York
1 CONT 
1 CONT Elizabeth died young in Ipswich
1 CONT 
1 CONT Bio:
1 CONT 
1 CONT Samuel Griffin was born about 1645 in Ipswich, Essex, Massachusetts. He died in the same town on October 23, 1691.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Samuel Griffin married Lydia Younglove about 1680 Ipswich, Massachusetts. Upon his death Lydia married Henry Witham on 23 October 1691. [1] She died on 1 November 1702 in Gloucester, Mass. [2]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Samuel Griffin, son of Hugh and Elizabeth Griffin, was born in Ipswich. He was still living there in 1677, when he took the oath of allegiance, and in 1684, when he had a wife Lydia and a daughter Elizabeth, the latter of whom died in the year las
1 CONC t mentioned. Samuel, the father, died probably not long afterward, and Mr. Babson in his "History of Gloucester" (Notes and Additions) is of the opinion that his widow "Lydia was the Lydia Griffin who became the second wife of Henry Witham, of Anni
1 CONC squam, Gloucester, October 23, 1691, and that she brought to her new home a son Samuel, then a boy, who, December 18, 1703, married Elizabeth, daughter of Samuel York, who was settled in that part of the town". [3]
1 CONT 
1 CONT The names of those receiving woodland in 1723 furnishes a good directory of the male inhabitants of the town in 1704, all who were residents at that period being included in the list of grantees as follows: ... Samuel Griffin ... [4]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Sources
1 CONT 1. Hugh GRIFFIN - GRIFFYN, case #9921, Sudbury, 1656, pg 3 of 5 (https://www.americanancestors.org/DB536/i/14472/9921-co3/0)
1 CONT 
1 CONT 2. Massachusetts: Vital Records, 1620-1850, Sudbury - V1, pg 60 (https://www.americanancestors.org/DB190/i/7806/60/142133094)
1 CONT 
