0 @N3776@ NOTE === Life Sketch ===
1 CONT END OF LINE ANCESTOR  Her maiden name is not known:  There is No Marriage record to prove her surname, everything is pure speculation without a primary source marriage record.
1 CONT Do not use her Find A Grave as an actual source for any information as there is no photograph of her tombstone to prove her death date and place.  Nor are there any factual sources to prove all of the other information on it.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Wikitree profile Elizabeth (Unknown) wife of William French (about 1604 - 1668). 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Elizabeth (Unknown) French
1 CONT Born about 1604 [uncertain] in England 
1 CONT Died 31 Mar 1668 at about age 64 in Billerica, Massachusetts Bay Colony 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Elizabeth French formerly [surname unknown] aka Symes, Symmes, Godfrey 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Daughter of [father unknown] and [mother unknown]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Wife of William French — married [date unknown] (to 31 Mar 1668) in England 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Mother of Elizabeth (French) Ellis, Mary (French) Hyde, John French, Sarah (French) Peake, Jacob French, Hannah (French) Brackett and Samuel French 
1 CONT 
1 CONT Elizabeth (Unknown) French migrated to New England during the Puritan Great Migration (1621-1640).
1 CONT 
1 CONT Uncertain Origins There is no evidence as to what Elizabeth's origins were. Listed in Other Last Names are two ideas: Godfrey and Symmes (Symes).
1 CONT 
1 CONT Biography
1 CONT Elizabeth _______ born about 1605 in England immigrated to New England with her husband William on the ship Defence, in 1635, along with their children. Enrolled as passengers on the Defence, 4 July 1635: William French, age 30; Elizabeth French, a
1 CONC ge 30; Francis French, age 10; Elizabeth French, age 6, Marie French, age 2 1/2; John French, age 5 months. Her husband was a tailor, and came to New England as one of the servants to Roger Harlakenden.[1]
1 CONT 
1 CONT The family settled in Cambridge. She and William were listed as members of the Cambridge Church "in full communion" in January 1658/9. [2] In 1652, William received a grant of land in the division of "Shaw Shine" later known as Billerica, but was s
1 CONC till styled as "of Cambridge" in 1656, so the family took some time to relocate.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Elizabeth died in Billerica 31 March 1668 ["Elizabeth wife of Lt. William, died on Mar. 31, 1668."] [3] and was probably buried there.[4]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Marriage and Children
1 CONT Assuming that Elizabeth was the first wife of William they were married by about 1629 [or 1625 if the passenger Francis French was their son] :[5]
1 CONT 
1 CONT Possibly: Francis French b abt 1625 England. No further record. [The passenger on the Defence, but not the same as Francis of Derby, CT]
1 CONT Elizabeth French, b. abt. 1629 England, m. Dedham, MA 19 Sep 1650 Richard Ellis, d. Dedham 21 Oct 1694
1 CONT Mary French, b. abt. 1633 England, d. Cambridge 27 May 1672, m. Jonathan Hyde, b. abt. 1626, d. Newton, MA 5 Oct 1711
1 CONT John French, b. abt. 1635 England, bp 1635 in Cambridge, Massachusetts d. Oct 1712, m(1) 21 Jun 1659 Abigail Coggan, d. 5 Apr 1662, m(2) 3 Jul 1663 Hannah Burrage, d.7 Jul 1667, m(3) 14 Jan 1667-8 Mary Rogers, d. 16 Jun 1677, m(4) 16 Jan 1677-8 Mar
1 CONC y (Littlefield) Kittresge, d. 1719
1 CONT Sarah French, b. Cambridge, MA 1638, d. 1694, m. Roxbury, MA 15 Aug 1660 Jonathan Peake (son Jonathan Peake and Dorcas French), [GM says daughter of Christopher Peake] b. 17 Dec 1637, d. Roxbury 2 Jun 1700
1 CONT Jacob French, b. Cambridge 16 Jan 163940, d. 20 May 1713, m(1) 20 Sep 1665 Mary Champney (dau Richard Champney), d. 1 Apr 1681, m(2) 30 Jul 1685 Mary Convers, d. 18 Jun 1686, m(3) Mary ____, d. 9 Jun 1709, m(4) Ruth ____, d. 6 Nov 1730 [4th wife no
1 CONC t in GM]
1 CONT Hannah French, b. Cambridge 12 Apr 1641, d. 20 Jun 1642 Cambridge[6]
1 CONT Hannah French, b. Cambridge 16 Feb 1644, m. Billerica, MA 6 Sep 1661 John Brackett. Died Billerica 9 May 1674.[7]
1 CONT Samuel French, b. Cambridge 3 Dec 1645, bur. 15 Jul 1646
1 CONT 
1 CONT Research Notes
1 CONT The Elizabeth Symmes/Simes Theory: Sarah Simes was a servant of Roger Harlakeden and a passenger on the Defence with William French and his wife Elizabeth. In her will Sarah Simes refers to William French as her loving brother. RC Anderson in the G
1 CONC reat Migration sketch of William French states that this seems to be a reference to a brother in the church rather than a familial relation. Meyerick points out that there is no conflicting evidence, but it's interesting that William had two daught
1 CONC ers named Sarah.
1 CONT 
1 CONT The Godfrey Theory: While not supported by any evidence, the suggestion that her LNAB was Godfrey comes from "Immigrant Ancestors A list of 2,500 Immigrants to America before 1750". Extracted from Volume VII. A Compendium of American Genealogy Edit
1 CONC ed by Frederick Adams Virkus, (1942) p 852 FamilySearch
1 CONT 
1 CONT Disputed Daughter: Rebecca French (1630-1647) was previously attached as a daughter. The connection was severed as no reliable sources could be found that suggested William French had a daughter Rebecca.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Maiden name?: Her current (Feb 2024) Findagrave memorial suggests a maiden name of Newes without source info.[4]
1 CONT 
